			<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
			<aktViide>111072026003</aktViide>
		</avaldamismarge>
		<joustumine>2026-08-01</joustumine>
	</muutmismarge>
	<sisu>
		<osa id="o1">
			<osaNr>1</osaNr>
			<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Part 1]]></kuvatavNr>
			<osaPealkiri>GENERAL PART</osaPealkiri>
			<peatykk id="ptk1">
				<peatykkNr>1</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 1]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>General Provisions</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para1">
					<paragrahvNr>1</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 1.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Aim of this Code</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para1lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The aim of this Code is to promote the development of sustainable high-quality built environment and to ensure safety as well as the appropriate functionality and usability of the built environment.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para2">
					<paragrahvNr>2</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 2.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application of this Code</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para2lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>This Code applies to construction works, their design, building, use and maintenance in so far as this is not governed by other laws, ratified treaties or EU legislation. This requirements of this Code regarding activities in a public water body apply equally to activities in the exclusive economic zone of sea areas.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para2lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>This Code does not apply to building work that is carried out forthwith due to an unavoidable and urgent need arising in connection with a rescue event, with countering a threat and eliminating a danger and with alleviating the consequences of a rescue event.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para2lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>This Code does not apply to extraction of mineral resources, unless the law governing the extraction of mineral resources provides otherwise.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para2lg3b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Unless otherwise provided by the Land Improvement Act, this Code does not apply to the building of land improvement systems.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-05-31</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>131052018003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-01-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para2lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Provisions of the Administrative Procedure Act apply to the administrative proceedings provided for by this Code without prejudice to special rules established by this Code.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para2lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>This Code applies to construction works that serve national defence purposes, to construction works of security authorities and to infrastructure at the national border, as well as to the design, building, use and upkeep of such construction works and infrastructure insofar as this does not contravene the State Secrets and Classified Information of Foreign States Act. This Code does not apply to the building of temporary construction works in the course of training events of the Defence Forces and of the Defence League.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para2lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Provisions of the Environmental Impact Assessment and Environmental Management System Act apply to the assessment of environmental impact of building work. Where possible, the procedures of environmental impact assessment is combined with the procedures provided for by this Code. In that case, the requirements established for both must be met.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para3">
					<paragrahvNr>3</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 3.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Construction work</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para3lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Construction work’ means a structure that is created as a result of human action and that is attached to or supported by the ground underneath and whose purpose of use, aim, manner of use or durability make it distinguishable from other structures.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para3lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A construction work is either a building or a civil engineering work. A building is a construction work that has an interior space that is separated from the external environment by the roof and other parts of the building envelope. A civil engineering work is any construction work other than a building.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para3lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para3lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Temporary construction work’ means a construction work that is built for a period of time that is shorter than five years and that is demolished after that period elapses.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para3lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the list of technical specifications concerning construction works and the principles of calculating these specifications, including the area occupied by the construction work and its height and depth.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para4">
					<paragrahvNr>4</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 4.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building work</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para4lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Building work [in this translation, also ‘the building of’]’ means the erection, construction, installation and demolition of a construction work and any other operations in relation to the construction work that lead to the creation of that construction work or to a change in its physical properties. ‘Building work’ also means the shifting of soil or paving layers to a degree that has a significant and permanent impact on the surrounding environment and is functionally related to the construction work.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para4lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Adding an extension to a construction work’ means building work in the course of which an existing construction work is modified by the building of an annex adjoining, abutting, overlying or underlying the construction work.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para4lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Remodelling – i.e., renovation – of a construction work’ means building work in the course of which the properties of the existing construction work are significantly altered. Replacement of specific elements of an existing construction work with equivalent elements is not regarded as remodelling. The remodelling of a construction work means, first and foremost, building work in the course of which:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para4lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the building's envelope elements are altered;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para4lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the building's loadbearing or stiffening elements are altered or replaced;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para4lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a utility system is installed, modified or demolished, which alters the external appearance or other properties of the construction work;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para4lg3p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the working parameters of the construction work or the technology used are significantly altered;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para4lg3p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the construction work is brought into conformity with the requirements corresponding to its purpose of use;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para4lg3p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a construction work that has been partially or completely destroyed is restored in essentially similar form.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para4lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Demolition of a construction work’ means building work in the course of which a construction work is partially or completely removed or dismantled. If the aim of demolition is to build, on the site of the demolished construction work, a new construction work that is essentially similar to the construction work that was demolished, this may be regarded as remodelling – i.e., restoration – of the construction work. If the aim of demolition is to build, on the site of the demolished construction work, an essentially new construction work, this is regarded as the demolition of one construction work and the building – i.e., erection or construction – of another. The construction work is deemed to be essentially similar to the previous construction work if its volume and purpose of use remain unchanged and its architectural solutions remain unchanged or undergo minimal change due to deployment of up-to-date building materials or utility systems or to compliance with the requirements for residential premises.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para4lg4b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The remodelling of utility network lines or of utility works is deemed to include, among other things, situations where the line or work is demolished and replaced by an essentially similar one. The utility network line or utility work is deemed to be essentially similar if its location remains unchanged and its protection zone unextended, the change in its height or volume is up to 33 per cent and its purpose of use and impact remain similar to those of the previous line or work.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para4lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Utility system’ means a set of equipment, installations or utility lines that are required for the functioning and use of the construction work and for ensuring its safety, including all structural elements required for the functioning of such equipment, installations or lines.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para5">
					<paragrahvNr>5</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 5.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building design documentation</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para5lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Building design documentation’ means a body of information that is created in the course of designing the construction work and that contains the information required to build the construction work. Where relevant, the building design documentation also reflects the information required for use and maintenance of the construction work.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para6">
					<paragrahvNr>6</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 6.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Maintenance of construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para6lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The maintenance (upkeep) of a construction work encompasses operations whose purpose is to preserve the state in which the construction work retains its functionality and usability and corresponds to the requirements that must be fulfilled in order for the construction work to comply with its designed purpose, or to restore the construction work to such a state.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para6b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">6</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 6<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Area of interest</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk2">
				<peatykkNr>2</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 2]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Principles and Principal Requirements</peatykkPealkiri>
				<jagu id="jg1">
					<jaguNr>1</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 1]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Principles</jaguPealkiri>
					<paragrahv id="para7">
						<paragrahvNr>7</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 7.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Good practice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para7lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Construction works must be designed, built and maintained according to good practice. Good practice must also be observed in pursuing any other actions or operations regulated by this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para8">
						<paragrahvNr>8</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 8.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Principle of safety</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para8lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Construction works, building work, the use of construction works and any other operations related to building work must be safe. Construction works, building work, the use of construction works and any other operations related to building work are safe if they do not create a danger to humans, property, the environment, national security or a national defence object. The safety of construction works and of building work encompasses the protection of valuable features of the natural environment and of items or structures of cultural significance and, where relevant, also the life and health of animals.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para9">
						<paragrahvNr>9</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 9.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Principle of environmental soundness</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para9lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Construction works, building work and the use of construction works must be as environmentally sound as possible – with preference given to retrofitting of construction works over the building of new ones – and the use of natural resources in the course of building work must be sparing. When designing a construction work, the impact of known changes in the climate must be taken into account.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para9lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Construction works, building work and the use of construction works must promote responsible land use, sustainable methods of mobility and the diversity, adaptability and reuse of the built environment.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para10">
						<paragrahvNr>10</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 10.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Principle of professionalism</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para10lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The principle of professionalism requires natural and legal persons to exercise due diligence in order to ensure that their actions are safe, comply with established requirements and lead to a result that conforms to the requirements. The prerequisites of professionalism are knowledge and skills that correspond to the specific character of the operations.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para10lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The principle of professionalism requires natural and legal persons pursuing an economic or professional activity to comply with the duty to give explanations. The duty to give explanations extends to giving information in relation to matters connected to the activity as well as informing the parties concerned of circumstances that affect the safety of the construction work, its conformity to established requirements and its purpose of use.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para10lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The principle of professionalism requires natural or legal persons pursuing an economic or professional activity to cooperate with other persons involved in the creation of the building design documentation and in the building work in order to ensure that building work is performed in a rational manner, the different parts of the building design documentation form a coherent whole, and all elements of the construction work function coherently in combination.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
				<jagu id="jg2">
					<jaguNr>2</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 2]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Principal Requirements for Constructions Works and Building Work</jaguPealkiri>
					<paragrahv id="para11">
						<paragrahvNr>11</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 11.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para11lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Construction works must comply with the requirements for their use throughout their entire useful life, and must remain safe throughout their entire existence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para11lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where relevant, the requirements for construction works encompass:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>structural integrity, including durability, constructive strength, serviceability and stability;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>fire safety, including the needs of evacuation and rescue;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p2b1">
								<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>construction of a shelter;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>hygienic conditions and protection from impacts harmful to health;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>safety of use and accessibility;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>noise protection and acoustic properties;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>energy conservation and energy efficiency;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>sparing use of natural resources;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p8b1">
								<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the passage of emissions from the construction work into the outdoor environment without harm to the latter;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the functionality of a construction work, its functional coherence and compatibility;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p10">
								<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements arising from the purpose of use and from use of the construction work – i.e., requirements concerning the state of the construction work, including maintenance requirements;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para11lg2p11">
								<alampunktNr>11</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[11)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the marking of the construction work and its location.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para11lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The requirements for construction works observe the basic requirements provided by Annex I of Regulation (EU) 2024/3110 of the European Parliament and of the Council laying down harmonised rules for the marketing of construction products and repealing Regulation (EU) No 305/2011 (OJ L, 2024/3110, 18.12.2024).<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para11lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may, by means of a regulation, specify the requirements for construction works ‒ except regarding the requirements provided by clause 2<sup>1</sup> of subsection 2 of this section.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 02.10.2025, 2  ‒ entry into force 01.07.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para11lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The Government of the Republic may, by means of a regulation, specify the requirements for construction works regarding the requirements provided by clause 2<sup>1</sup> of subsection 2 of this section.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 02.10.2025, 2  ‒ entry into force 01.07.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para12">
						<paragrahvNr>12</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 12.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for building work</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para12lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Building work must be carried out according to building design documentation and in conformity with the requirements for construction works and with the requirements for building work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para12lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A construction work that is being built and, where relevant, also the corresponding building work, must conform to the restrictions and spatial plans applicable by reason of its location. In the absence of a detailed spatial plan, such a construction work must conform to the comprehensive spatial plan and, where the obligation to obtain design specifications applies, to the design specifications. In situations provided for by the Spatial Planning Act, the construction work must conform to the national or municipal designated spatial plan.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para12lg2b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In situations where this is justified, the competent authority may allow the building of a temporary construction work on an item of immovable property regardless of the fact that the property’s main intended purpose of use according to the comprehensive spatial plan – or the plot’s intended purpose of use according to the detailed spatial plan, or the intended purpose of use of the cadastral unit – does not match the purpose of use of the construction work, provided that the main intended purpose of use of the area according to the comprehensive plan remains the predominant use and, where a detailed spatial plan exists, the possibility to implement the integral solution provided by that plan is ensured.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para12lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>While carrying out building work, the rights of the persons affected by the building work must be taken into consideration and steps must be taken to avoid excessive harm to such rights.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para12lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The properties of the products used in carrying out building work must be such that make it possible for the construction work to comply with the requirements during a reasonable period of time; this includes the obligation to ensure, when natural building materials that have not been processed industrially, or native construction products manufactured in a traditional way, or recovered construction products are incorporated in the construction work in a permanent manner, that construction works comply with the requirements. The requirements for construction products are provided by Regulation (EU) 305/2011 of the European Parliament and of the Council, and in the Product Conformity Act and the legislation enacted under that Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para12lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may, by means of a regulation, establish requirements for building work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para13">
						<paragrahvNr>13</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 13.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for building design documentation</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para13lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Building design documentation must be such that the construction work built according to that documentation complies with the requirements; this includes taking into account the suitability and usability of the construction work and its need for maintenance.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para13lg1b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When assessing the suitability of the construction work – based on the nature of that construction work – regard must be had to the particular characteristics and context of its location and its functional and aesthetic fit with the surrounding space.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para13lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Building design documentation must be such that it is possible to build according to that documentation, to check the conformity of the construction work and of building work to the requirements and, where relevant, also to use and maintain the construction work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para13lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, requirements for the filing, content and form of building design documentation.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para14">
						<paragrahvNr>14</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 14.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Creation and verification of building design documentation</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para14lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The following must be taken into account when creating building design documentation:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the requirements established for the construction work, including special requirements arising from its purpose of use;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>relevant site investigations, risk analyses and other circumstances pertaining to the location of the construction work;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the spatial plan or design specifications where they exist or where their existence is mandatory;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg1p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>restrictions arising from public law by reason of the location of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg1p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements of the building process.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para14lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is needed, site investigations must be conducted in order to obtain important technical information required for the creation of the building design documentation. Site investigations may also include assessing the impact of the construction work and of building work on other construction works. The results of site investigations must be filed with the Register of Construction Works and, in situations provided for by legislation, to other databases or administrative bodies. The results of site investigations should be preferably filed in an electronic form.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para14lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Before the commencement of building work, the conformity to the requirements of the building design documentation according to which the building work is to be carried out must be verified by a competent person who is independent of the person who created the building design documentation and who performs an expert assessment where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the planned construction work is complicated in terms of its engineering, or for other reasons possesses an increased potential to become a danger or</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the authority performing construction supervision has reasonable doubts as to the conformity of the building design documentation to the requirements, such as when the building design documentation has not been created by a person who meets the relevant qualification requirements.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para14lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg4p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements for the expert assessment of building design documentation, and for the filing and preservation of such assessments, including specific criteria for identifying construction works whose building design documentation must undergo expert assessment;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para14lg4p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements for site investigations, and for the filing and preservation of such investigations, including requirements for their specific datasets and the form in which their results must be presented.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para15">
						<paragrahvNr>15</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 15.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Documentation of building work</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para15lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is provided for by legislation, building work must be documented. Building work must always be documented where a building permit is required for carrying out such work. Building work is documented by the person who performs it.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para15lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The documents that characterise building work (hereinafter, <i>building documentation</i>) must provide information on the construction work and on the building work performed that is relevant for using the construction work and for verifying the conformity of the construction work to the requirements, including information regarding the construction products and materials used. The building documentation must contain information that permits identification of the person responsible for the building work performed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para15lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Building documentation primarily consists of:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para15lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>as-built drawings or as-built model;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para15lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a journal of building operations;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para15lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>reports of covered work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para15lg3p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>minutes of work meetings;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para15lg3p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>any other documents that characterise the building work, including equipment and utility system setup and testing logs and installation manuals.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para15lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Building documentation must be handed over to the Register of Construction Works, to the municipality or another competent authority designated by legislation. The documents should be preferably handed over in an electronic form.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para15lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para15lg5p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements for the documentation of building work and for documents reflecting such work;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para15lg5p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements for documents reflecting building work, for their handover and preservation, specifying the documents that must be handed over.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para16">
						<paragrahvNr>16</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 16.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for the use and maintenance of construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para16lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>During the existence of the construction work, its safe condition and, where relevant, good upkeep must be ensured.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para16lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The construction work must be used prudently and according to its purpose of use. During the time of use of the construction work, the professional maintenance required for the continued stability and safe use of the construction work must be ensured.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para16lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The requirements for the use and maintenance of the construction work emanate from good practices, legislation or from the instructions for maintenance (hereinafter, <i>maintenance instructions</i>) compiled for the construction work.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para16lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may, by means of a regulation, enact requirements concerning the maintenance of construction works.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para17">
						<paragrahvNr>17</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 17.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Maintenance instructions</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para17lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Maintenance instructions contain the maintenance requirements prescribed by the manufacturer of the utility system, device, product or special-care structure or material, taking into account the particular characteristics of use of the construction work. Maintenance instructions may also contain information regarding the use of the construction work, regarding the mandatory or voluntary nature of its audit and any other information needed for its maintenance.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para17lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Maintenance instructions are issued by the person who designed or built the construction work or by another competent person. Where modifications are made to the construction work, the maintenance instructions must be amended if this is needed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para17lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Unless otherwise provided by legislation, the existence of maintenance instructions is not mandatory. The existence of maintenance instructions or the compliance with the requirements and performance of operations specified in such instructions does not preclude the responsibility of the owner in relation to any dangers arising from the construction work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para17lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Maintenance instructions must be electronically transmitted to the Register of Construction Works and, in situations provided for by legislation, also to other registers or competent authorities.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para17lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may, by regulation, enact requirements concerning maintenance instructions, their filing and preservation, including requirements regarding updates to such instructions, and may also specify situations where maintenance instructions are required.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para18">
						<paragrahvNr>18</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 18.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Audits of construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para18lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The aim of the audit of a construction work is to prove that the construction work conforms to the requirements and that it is safe to use the construction work for its intended purpose and in the intended manner, or to provide another assessment concerning the construction work. Audits of construction works fall into pre-use, regular and extraordinary audits.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para18lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is provided by legislation, a pre-use audit of the construction work must be performed prior to commencement of the use of the construction work and a regular or extraordinary audit must be performed in the specified instances when the construction work is in use.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para18lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The person who performs the audit of a construction work must be competent and independent and ensure the uniformity and reliability of the auditing process.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para18lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The person who performs the audit of a construction work may not be connected to the owner, designer or builder of the construction work, to the manufacturer of a construction product incorporated into the construction work, to the importer or distributor of such a product and to the person who installed the product in a degree that would cast doubt on the independence and impartiality of the performer of the audit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para18lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, requirements for audits of construction works, for the methods of such audits,for the filing and preservation of audits, as well as the instances and frequency of regular and extraordinary audits.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
				<jagu id="jg3">
					<jaguNr>3</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 3]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Obligations of Persons when Performing Certain Duties Related to Construction</jaguPealkiri>
					<paragrahv id="para19">
						<paragrahvNr>19</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 19.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Obligations of the owner</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para19lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The owner must ensure the conformity of the construction work, of building work and of the use of the construction work to the requirements arising from legislation; amongst other things, the owner must ensure:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para19lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the conformity of the construction work to spatial plans or to design specifications;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para19lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the existence of permits required for building work and for the use and occupancy of the construction work and the making of the required notifications and notices;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para19lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>that any work that is performed directly at the owner's instruction and that is governed by this Code is performed by a person possessing sufficient skills and knowledge (hereinafter, <i>qualifications</i>) that correspond to the specific character of the work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para19lg1p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the maintenance and safety of use of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para19lg1p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>owner oversight in situations provided for by law.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para19lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the owner themselves creates building design documentation, performs building work or owner oversight or any other work governed by this Code, they must observe the principle of professionalism and ensure conformity of the work to the requirements; where relevant, this includes the obligation to document the building work.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para19lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where a corporate owner itself builds – or creates building design documentation for – a construction work that is subject to the building permit requirement, it is subject to to the same requirements that apply to persons performing this work in the course of their economic activities; among other things, its qualifications must be proven by a professional qualification based on education and work experience that conforms to the Professions Act or a certificate of competence issued under other legislation.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para20">
						<paragrahvNr>20</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 20.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Owner oversight of construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para20lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The owner is obligated to ensure competent oversight (hereinafter, <i>owner oversight</i>) of the building work performed when building a construction work.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para20lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The person performing owner oversight may not, as part of their economic activity, be connected to any other operations related to the same construction work, or to any persons whose work they oversee.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para20lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the person performing owner oversight lacks the skills or knowledge to perform supervision over certain operations, a competent person is instructed to perform supervision over such operations. Responsibility for the actions of the instructed person lies with the party who instructed them.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para20lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The performance of owner oversight does not preclude or restrict the contractor's responsibility under the contract for services.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para20lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the rules for performing owner oversight.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para21">
						<paragrahvNr>21</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 21.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Obligations of undertakings</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para21lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A person who performs duties related to construction as part of their economic activity (hereinafter, <i>undertaking</i>) must in their actions observe the principles and requirements provided by laws; amongst other things, the undertaking must:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para21lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>observe the principle of professionalism and ensure that the persons operating under its responsibility possess sufficient qualifications and that each particular project or site is assigned a competent person in charge of that project or site;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para21lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>ensure that operations performed under its responsibility and governed by this Code are documented according to the requirements and that relevant documents are handed over to the competent authority following applicable rules;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para21lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>comply with the requirements established in the General Part of the Economic Activities Code Act; this includes the requirements established with regard to service providers.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para21lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>An undertaking assumes responsibility for the actions of persons who act in the undertaking's interests if the undertaking uses such persons to perform its obligations and the actions of the persons acting in the undertaking's interests are connected to the performance of such obligations.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para21lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The obligations that this Code provides for undertakings do not affect the undertaking's contractual obligations or any other obligations that the undertaking may have under the Law of Obligations Act. In the event of a conflict between a contractual obligation and an obligation arising from this Code, the obligation arising from this Code takes precedence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para22">
						<paragrahvNr>22</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 22.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Competence of undertakings</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para22lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The undertaking must have the competence to perform any work it undertakes in a professional manner. The undertaking may not provide misleading information regarding its competence and may not perform work that it is not competent to perform.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para22lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competence of the undertaking corresponds to the qualifications of the persons acting in the undertaking's interests and under the undertaking's responsibility.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para22lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The undertaking ensures that it is possible for the competent person to do their work with the due diligence that corresponds to the specific character of the work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para22lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority issuing building permits or the authority performing construction supervision may prohibit or suspend building work or refuse to issue a building permit until a sufficiently qualified person is appointed to manage the building work or to scrutinise the building design documentation, provided the lack of competence would have precluded professional performance of the work and given rise to danger.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para23">
						<paragrahvNr>23</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 23.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Competent person</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para23lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A competent person performs, scrutinises or manages work independently in an area of activity related to their competence and assumes responsibility for such work, files technical opinions in their own name or, when acting in the interests of an undertaking, in the name of the undertaking, and, where this is needed, arranges the allocation of resources and organises the work of others.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para23lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A person is competent if they hold a qualification that corresponds to the specific character of the work. It is prohibited to provide misleading information regarding one's qualifications and to perform work that one is not qualified to perform.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para23lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A competent person performs their tasks professionally and with the due diligence that corresponds to the specific character of the work; amongst other things, a competent person may not act as the competent person for several undertakings or be in charge of several sites if the resulting workload would not permit the competent person to perform their tasks as required.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para23lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A person who holds a professional certificate or a certificate of competency is deemed to be qualified to perform any work covered by the certificate.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para23lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In situations provided for by and in relation to the areas of activity specified in this Code, the qualification of the competent person must be certified.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para23lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this Code does not provide the qualification requirements for operating in a specific area of activity, including the manner of proving one's qualification, the suitability of the person's qualification is assessed first and foremost, if the person operates as an undertaking, by the owner of the construction work or by the party commissioning the person’s services and, if the person is an employee or a subcontractor of an undertaking, the undertaking.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para23lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may, by regulation, enact recommended requirements for areas of activity in the field of construction.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para24">
						<paragrahvNr>24</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 24.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for certain areas of activity</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para24lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In situations mentioned in this section, the undertaking and the competent person may provide their services and perform duties in the field of construction as part of their economic activity if the qualification of the competent person who acts in the interests and under the responsibility of the undertaking is proved by means of a professional certificate issued on the basis of the relevant education and work experience in accordance with the Professions Act or by means of a certificate of competency issued under other legislation.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para24lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The qualification of the competent person must be proved in the following areas of activity:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the building of construction works subject to the building permit requirement;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>creation of building design documentation of construction works subject to the building permit requirement;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of owner oversight;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the issuing of energy performance certificates;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of energy audits;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of site investigations;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of expert assessment of building design documentation;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the auditing of construction works;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>construction and installation of heating appliances that use solid fuel and of chimneys and flue vent connectors;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p10">
								<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>chimney sweeping;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p11">
								<alampunktNr>11</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[11)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of road safety audits;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p12">
								<alampunktNr>12</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[12)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the maintenance of public roads;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg2p13">
								<alampunktNr>13</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[13)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the creation of design documentation concerning traffic arrangements.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para24lg2b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When active in the area of activity of road safety audits mentioned in clause 11 of subsection 2 of this section, the proven qualification of the competent person presumes completion of the curriculum mentioned in clause 5 of subsection 2 of § 102 of this Code and re-completion of the curriculum after every seven-year period.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para24lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the person has acquired the qualification corresponding to the specific character of the work in a foreign state, they are not required to prove their qualification by means of a professional certificate issued in accordance with the Professions Act or of a certificate of competency issued under other legislation. The correspondence of the qualification acquired in a foreign state to the requirements provided by this Code is assessed and certified, in accordance with the Recognition of Foreign Professional Qualifications Act, by:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the Transport Administration in the field of road building and in the area of activity of road safety audits;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para24lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the Rescue Board in the areas of activity mentioned in clauses 9 and 10 of subsection 2 of this section.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para24lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In the area of activity set out in clause 2 of subsection 2 of this section, ‘competent person’ also means an architect who has acquired their professional qualification in a member state of the European Economic Area or in the Swiss Confederation, which is proved by a document mentioned in paragraphs 3–5 of Article 23, in Article 49 and in Annexes V and VI of Directive 2005/36/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council of 7 September 2005 on the recognition of professional qualifications (OJ L 255, 30.09.2005, pp. 22–142).</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-07-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>110072020003</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2020-07-15</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para24lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, detailed divisions of the areas of activity provided for by subsection 2 of this section.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2021-11-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>2</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130112021002</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-04-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para24lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2021-11-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>2</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130112021002</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-04-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para25">
						<paragrahvNr>25</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 25.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Notification obligation</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para25lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A notice of economic activities must be filed with the Register of Economic Activities by the undertakings who operate in the following areas of activity:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the building of construction works subject to the building permit requirement, except where the work of the competent person of the undertaking does not involve managing and arranging the work of others;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the designing of construction works subject to the building permit requirement;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of owner oversight;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of site investigations;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the performance of expert assessment of building design documentation;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the auditing of construction works, except where the undertaking is an accreditation body accredited for the auditing of construction works in accordance with Regulation (EC) No. 765/2008 of the European Parliament and of the Council setting out the requirements for accreditation and market surveillance relating to the marketing of products and repealing Regulation (EEC) No. 339/93 (OJ L 218, 13.08.2008, pp. 30–47);</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the maintenance of public roads;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para25lg1p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the creation of design documentation concerning traffic arrangements.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para25lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In addition to the information provided for by the General Part of the Economic Activities Code Act, the notice of economic activity sets out the specific activity within the area of activity as provided by a regulation enacted under subsection 4 of § 24 of this Code, and the information specified in subsection 2 of § 15 of the General Part of the Economic Activities Code Act with regard to the competent person of the undertaking.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para25lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The notification of an economic activity is deemed to have been filed when a confirmation by the competent person regarding their legal relationship with the undertaking is recorded in the Register of Economic Activities. A competent person may not, at any time, act as the competent person of more than three undertakings.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para25lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the notice mentioned in subsection 1 of § 58 of the General Part of the Economic Activities Code Act is not filed via the Estonian information portal, it is filed together with the consent of the competent person with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority who enters the information included in the notice and the competent person's consent in the Register of Economic Activities.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para25lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the competent person does not file their consent or withdrawal of consent via the Estonian information portal, they file it with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority who enters the consent or withdrawal of consent in the Register of Economic Activities.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para25lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In the event of severance of the legal relationship between the competent person and the undertaking, the competent person is entitled to withdraw their consent. If the competent person has withdrawn their consent, the undertaking must file with the registrar a notice concerning changes in the general information regarding economic activities in accordance with subsection 5 of § 30 of the General Part of the Economic Activities Code Act. If the competent person who has withdrawn their consent is the only competent person of the undertaking with regard to the specific activity within an area of activity, the undertaking is deemed not to comply with the notification obligation with regard to that specific activity.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk3">
				<peatykkNr>3</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 3]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Design Specifications</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para26">
					<paragrahvNr>26</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 26.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Design specifications when creation of detailed spatial plan is not mandatory</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para26lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are needed to create building design documentation for buildings subject to the building permit requirement or for civil engineering works of significant public interest (hereinafter, <i>significant civil engineering works</i>) in situations where the creation of a detailed spatial plan is not mandatory, or in other situations provided for by law.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para26lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority issues design specifications:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for the erection or creation of buildings or significant civil engineering works;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for the expansion of buildings or significant civil engineering works by more than 33 per cent of their original volume.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para26lg2b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority may, on an application from a person, also issue design specifications in situations not mentioned in subsections 1 and 2 of this section.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para26lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When issuing design specifications, consideration must be given to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the environment that has become established around the building or significant civil engineering work, including the types of building characteristic of the area;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the avoidance of breaches of legislation or harm to the rights of persons or to the public interest;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements established in the spatial plan;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg3p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>special requirements of heritage conservation, if these are required under the Heritage Conservation Act;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-03-19</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>13</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>119032019013</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2019-05-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg3p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the principle provided by § 8 of the Spatial Planning Act.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para26lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>With regard to the building or significant civil engineering work, the design specifications establish, where relevant:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>its purpose of use;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the maximum number permitted to be built in a land area;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>its location;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the maximum ground projection area that the building or significant civil engineering work may occupy;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>its height and, where relevant, depth;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements concerning architectural solution, building work and appearance;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the possible location of the construction work needed to service ithe building or significant civil engineering work;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the need for site investigations;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p9">
							<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the principles for planting vegetation, for street-side maintenance and for traffic arrangements;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para26lg4p10">
							<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the time limit for demolishing the building or civil engineering work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para26lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If it becomes known in the process of issuing design specifications that their bringing into effect may entail the need to subject an item of immovable property or a part of such an item to acquisition in the public interest, including to compulsory acquisition, or compulsory possession, the competent authority informs the owner of the item within seven days following the date on which the need to subject the item to acquisition in the public interest, including to compulsory acquisition – or to impose compulsory possession on the item – came to light.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-06-29</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>129062018001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2018-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para26b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">26</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 26<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Design specifications where a national or local designated spatial plan is present</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para26b1lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are required to approve the building design documentation created to build any construction works based on a national or local designated spatial plan brought into effect following a pre-selection of the location for the construction works in question.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2025-07-08</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>6</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>108072025006</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2025-07-18</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para26b1lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When issuing the design specifications mentioned in subsection 1 of this section, clauses 2 and 4 of subsection 3 of § 26 of this Code are followed and the requirements mentioned in subsection 4 are determined.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para27">
					<paragrahvNr>27</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 27.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Issuing design specifications in a situation where a detailed spatial plan exists</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para27lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where a detailed spatial plan exists, the competent authority may, if this is justified, issue design specifications for creation of building design documentation for a building dealt with by the plan, provided that:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>more than five years have passed since the adoption of the detailed spatial plan;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>since the bringing into effect of the plan, significant new circumstances have come to light or a material change has taken place in the spatial planning area or in that area’s impact area, due to which the plan can no longer be fully implemented, or<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>after the adoption of the detailed spatial plan, the relevant legislation has been amended or spatial plans have been adopted that significantly affect the implementation of the detailed spatial plan.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para27lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When issuing design specifications, consideration must be given to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the environment that has become established around the building or significant civil engineering work, including the types of building characteristic of the area;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the avoidance of breaches of legislation or harm to the rights of persons or to the public interest;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements established in the spatial plan;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>special requirements of heritage conservation provided by the detailed spatial plan, if these are required under the Heritage Conservation Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-03-19</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>13</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>119032019013</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2019-05-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para27lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Under subsection 1 of this section, design specifications are not issued to change the nature of the spatial planning solution established by the detailed spatial plan, to provide further specification regarding a detailed spatial plan that amends the comprehensive spatial plan – in the part amending the latter –, for construction works that are to be built in a public water body and that have a permanent connection to the shore or are functionally connected to the shore, or to supplement a national or municipal designated spatial plan.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para27lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where relevant, the design specifications specify the provision made in the detailed spatial plan regarding:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the shares of the plot’s land use purposes, provided that those purposes have been prescribed for that plot in the detailed spatial plan;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the area to be occupied by buildings and the surface projection area of buildings, but not more than by 15 per cent of the initial solution;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>regarding the height – or, where needed, depth – of buildings whose height is below or above 20 metres, by, respectively, three metres or by 15 per cent of the initial solution;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p3b1">
							<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the number of the building’s storeys;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements concerning architectural solution, building work and appearance;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the possible location of a construction work needed to service the construction work situated in the land area, and the type of the civil engineering work;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p5b1">
							<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the number of buildings needed to service the construction work situated in the land area;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the need for site investigations;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the principles for planting vegetation, for streetside maintenance or for traffic arrangements;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para27lg4p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the boundaries of the plots in the spatial planning area, provided that the building rights initially granted in the area remain unchanged.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para27lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If it becomes known in the process of issuing design specifications that their bringing into effect may entail the need to subject an item of immovable property or part of such an item to acquisition in the public interest, including to compulsory acquisition, or compulsory possession, the competent authority informs the owner of the item within seven days following the date on which the need to subject the item to acquisition in the public interest, including to compulsory acquisition – or to impose compulsory possession on the item – came to light.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-06-29</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>129062018001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2018-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para28">
					<paragrahvNr>28</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 28.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Competent authority issuing design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para28lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are issued by the municipality unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para28lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where design specifications are issued on the basis of a national designated spatial plan based on the pre-selection of the location, the specifications are issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, unless otherwise provided for by law.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2025-07-08</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>6</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>108072025006</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2025-07-18</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para29">
					<paragrahvNr>29</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 29.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Application for design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para29lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The application for design specifications and the related documents are filed electronically with the competent authority via the Register of Construction Works. Where it is not possible to file these documents via the Register, they are filed with the competent authority and the competent authority enters the relevant information in the Register.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para29lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The application for design specifications states, first and foremost:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para29lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the applicant's name, contact information, signature and the date of the filing of the application;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para29lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the manner of delivery to the applicant of the design specifications;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para29lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the particulars and cadastral code of the item of immovable property on which building work is envisaged;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para29lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the aim of applying for the design specifications, including a description of the envisaged construction work or the type of building work to be performed in relation to it, and the possible location of the construction work or building work on the item of immovable property;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para29lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>information regarding payment of the statutory fee.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para29lg2p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>other requisite information.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para29lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the requirements concerning the form of the application and the form of design specifications and the rules for issuing design specifications.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para30">
					<paragrahvNr>30</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 30.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Checking the application for design specifications and refusal to consider the application</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para30lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When the competent authority receives an application for design specifications, it checks the conformity of the application to the requirements. Where it is manifest that the issuing of design specifications is impossible, the competent authority refuses to consider the application and returns it, stating the reasons for refusal. Above all, consideration of the application is refused and the application is returned if the grounds mentioned in subsection 1 of § 26 or subsection 1 of § 27 of this Code do not apply.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para31">
					<paragrahvNr>31</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 31.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Procedure for issuing design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para31lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority may decide to conduct proceedings for the issue of design specfications under the rules of open procedure. In a situation mentioned in subsection 5 of § 125 of the Spatial Planning Act, the rules of open procedure must be followed.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para31lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority issues the proposed design specifications and, primarily by electronic means, arranges the gathering of opinions and the giving of approvals concerning the proposed specifications, and issues the design specifications within 30 days from the filing of the application. If the competent authority decides to conduct open proceedings, the design specifications are issued within 60 days from the filing. The competent authority sets a time limit of up to ten days to give its approval or express an opinion.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para31lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the application is not filed by the owner of the item of immovable property named in the application, the competent authority adds that owner to the proceedings and, if this is needed, also adds to the proceedings the owners of adjacent items.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para31lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where this is needed, the competent authority refers the proposed design specifications:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para31lg4p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for approval to the authority in whom the law vests competencies that are related to the subject matter of the application for design specifications;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para31lg4p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for an opinion to the authority or person whose rights or interests may be affected by the construction work or building work envisaged in the application.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para31lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If observations are filed concerning the proposed design specifications in the course of the giving of approvals and opinions, the competent authority takes appropriate consideration of these observations or states the reasons for not taking them into consideration.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para31lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If the authority whose approval or the person or authority whose opinion is requested has not, within ten days from receiving the proposed design specifications, refused to give the approval or opinion or applied for an extension of that time limit, the proposed specifications are deemed to have been tacitly approved by the authority or the person or authority is deemed to have declined to express an opinion regarding them, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para32">
					<paragrahvNr>32</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 32.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Refusal to issue design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para32lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority refuses to issue design specifications if:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the creation of a spatial plan has been initiated and in connection with that a temporary building ban has been established;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the application for design specifications does not conform to the spatial plan;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the application for design specifications does not meet the criteria established in § 27 of this Code;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the application for design specifications does not conform to public-law restrictions provided by legislation or applicable by reason of the location of the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the construction work envisaged according to the design specifications may excessively infringe the rights of a third party;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the authority named in clause 1 of subsection 4 of § 31 of this Code has refused to approve the proposed design specifications and it is not possible to amend them;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the construction work envisaged according to the design specifications entails a significant environmental impact, which cannot be sufficiently avoided or alleviated;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>in applying for design specifications, knowingly false information has been filed that has an impact on the decision on issuing the design specifications, or</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para32lg1p9">
							<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the design specifications are sought to specify the details of the national or local designated spatial plan.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para33">
					<paragrahvNr>33</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 33.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Validity of design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para33lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are valid for five years. Where this is warranted by the circumstances, the competent authority may establish a different validity period or modify the validity period of the design specifications issued.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para33lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The design specifications issued earlier concerning the same subject matter are rendered invalid by the issuing of new design specifications in the matter.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para34">
					<paragrahvNr>34</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 34.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Revocation of design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para34lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority may revoke design specifications where:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para34lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the possibility of revocation is provided for by the specifications;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para34lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the data or the spatial plan based on which the specifications were issued have changed or other requirements for the relevant construction work and building work have changed;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para34lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a detailed spatial plan has subsequently been established in respect of the relevant item of immovable property;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para34lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a building ban has been established with regard to the item of immovable property that is within the subject matter of the application for design specifications;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para34lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>in applying for the specifications, knowingly false information has been filed that had an impact on the decision their issue.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk4">
				<peatykkNr>4</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 4]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Building Notice and Building Permit</peatykkPealkiri>
				<jagu id="jg4">
					<jaguNr>1</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 1]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Building Notice</jaguPealkiri>
					<paragrahv id="para35">
						<paragrahvNr>35</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 35.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Building notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para35lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In situations provided for by this section, the competent authority must be notified of building work prior to commencement of the work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para35lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The building notice is filed with the municipality, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para35lg2b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The building notice is filed with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority if the basis for building the construction work is provided by a national designated spatial plan or if building the construction work is related to building a construction work that conforms to such a plan.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para35lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The filing of a building notice is required regarding the construction works mentioned in Annex 1 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para35lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is warranted by the circumstances, the competent authority is authorised to demand the filing of a building notice concerning a construction work that is not included in Annex 1 to this Code. When considering whether to demand the filing of such a notice, the danger posed by the construction work and its impact on public space and on the rights of individuals is taken into account and a comparison is made with any similar indications provided by Annex 1 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para35lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the building design documentation of a construction work subject to the building permit requirement includes construction works whose building is subject to the notification obligation, the filing of the building permit application functions as the filing of the building notice.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para35lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the requirements concerning the form of building notices and the rules for their filing.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para36">
						<paragrahvNr>36</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 36.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Filing a building notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para36lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority is notified of the building of a construction work electronically via the Register of Construction Works. If notification via the Register is not possible, a building notice is filed with the competent authority, who enters the corresponding information in the Register.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para36lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A building notice must be filed at least ten days before the building of the construction work commences. If, within ten days from the filing of the building notice, the competent authority does not inform the person who filed the building notice of the need for further verification of the information presented in the building notice, building work may commence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para36lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A building notice states:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the name, contact information and signature of the person filing the notice, the desired manner of the document's delivery and the date of the filing;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the particulars and cadastral code of the item of immovable property on which building work is to be performed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the aim of filing the notice, including a description of the envisaged construction work and the type of building work, the location of the construction work on the item of immovable property and its purpose of use;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg3p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where the notice concerns a temporary construction work, the period of time envisaged for using the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg3p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where required, the energy performance certificate.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para36lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is mentioned in Annex 1 of this Code, the building notice must be accompanied by the relevant building design documentation.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para36lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is needed, the competent authority carries out a verification of whether, in relation to the construction work or building work stated in the building notice, it is necessary:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg5p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to bring the construction work or building work into compliance with the requirements;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg5p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to obtain the approval of the competent authority for the construction work or building work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg5p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to establish further requirements for the construction work with regard to its architectural or engineering solution or appearance;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para36lg5p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to add the owner of the item of immovable property or owners of adjacent items to the proceedings.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para36lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the grounds provided by subsection 5 of this section apply, the rules established in relation to building permits are observed; this includes the time limit for issuing building permits and the grounds for refusal to issue a building permit. The requirements presented as a result of the verification are issued by the competent authority as an administrative decision.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para37">
						<paragrahvNr>37</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 37.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Commencement of building work based on a building notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para37lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The building of a construction work on the basis of the building notice may take place within four years following the filing of the building notice or issue – in the form of an administrative decision – of requirements presented as the result of an inspection, or of approval of the building design documentation.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
				<jagu id="jg5">
					<jaguNr>2</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 2]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Building Permit</jaguPealkiri>
					<paragrahv id="para38">
						<paragrahvNr>38</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 38.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para38lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A building permit grants a right to build a construction work that corresponds to the building design documentation based on which the building permit is issued.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para38lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A building permit is required where this is mentioned in Annex 1 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para38lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is warranted by the circumstances, the competent authority is authorised to issue a building permit or to demand that a building permit be issued in respect of a construction work not included in Annex 1 to this Code. When considering whether to issue the building permit, the danger posed by the construction work and its impact on public space and on the rights of individuals is taken into account and a comparison is made with the similar indications provided by Annex 1 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para39">
						<paragrahvNr>39</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 39.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Authority competent to issue a building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para39lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The building permit is issued by the municipality, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para39lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the application for a building permit includes construction works which are to be built on the basis of a national designated spatial plan or whose building is related to the building of a construction work that conforms to such a plan, the building permit is issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, unless otherwise provided by law.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para39lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the application for a building permit includes construction works in respect of which the issuing of the building permit is in the competency of the state and of the municipality, the corresponding building permit is issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para39lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the application for a building permit includes construction works in respect of which the issuing of the building permit is in the competency of several government agencies, the corresponding building permit is issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para40">
						<paragrahvNr>40</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 40.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Application for a building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para40lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a building permit and the related documents are filed with the competent authority electronically via the Register of Construction Works. Where it is not possible to file these documents via the Register, they are filed with the competent authority who enters the information in the Register.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para40lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a building permit states:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the applicant's name, contact information and signature, and the date of the filing;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the manner of delivery of the building permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the particulars and cadastral code of the item of immovable property on which building work is to be performed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the aim of applying for the building permit, including the description and purpose of use of the envisaged construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where the application concerns a temporary construction work, the period of time envisaged for using the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the particulars of the person who created the building design documentation; where the conformity of the building design documentation to the requirements was verified by a competent person who is independent of the person who created the building design documentation, also the particulars of that competent person;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where required, the energy performance certificate;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para40lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>information regarding payment of the statutory fee.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para40lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a building permit must be accompanied by building design documentation that conforms to the requirements. If an expert assessment has been conducted to verify the conformity of the building design documentation to the requirements, the expert assessment report must also be filed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para40lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the requirements concerning the form of the application for a building permit and of the building permit, and the rules governing the filing of applications for a building permit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para41">
						<paragrahvNr>41</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 41.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Checking an application for a building permit and refusing to consider the application</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para41lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When the competent authority receives an application for a building permit, it checks the conformity of the application to the requirements. Where it is manifest that the issuing of the building permit is impossible, the competent authority refuses to consider the application and returns it, stating the reasons for the refusal.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para42">
						<paragrahvNr>42</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 42.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Procedure for issuing building permits</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para42lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The building permit is issued if the building design documentation that has been filed conforms to the requirements established in legislation, i.e., above all to the detailed spatial plan or design specifications and to the requirements for construction works and for building work. Where this is provided for by law, the construction work must conform to the national or municipal designated spatial plan.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority decides on the need to initiate the assessment of environmental impact.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>By way of ancillary requirements, the building permit may, above all, stipulate the following:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>restriction of the validity period of the building permit to the time limit for demolishing the temporary construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg3p1b1">
								<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the time limit for demolishing the construction work and, where this is needed, requirements concerning the post-demolition situation - where the ground for setting the time limit emanates from a legislative instrument or from a spatial plan;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the possibility of varying the building permit, where several building permits have been issued in respect of the same item of immovable property and are valid;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the possibility of varying the period of validity of the building permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg3p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the possibility of repeated installation of the same construction work in the same location - or in the area defined in the building permit - without filing a building notice or building permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg3p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>additional requirements for building work due to the complexity of the construction work or of the building process or</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg3p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the conduct of an expert assessment of the building design documentation.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is warranted by the circumstances, the competent authority is entitled to require the conduct of site investigations or of further investigations to elaborate the results of earlier investigations. The results of site investigations must be taken into account when creating building design documentation.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority issues the building permit within 30 days from the date of filing the application. The competent authority sets a time limit of up to ten days for the giving of approvals or opinions.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the application is not filed by the owner of the item of immovable property named in the application, the competent authority adds that owner to the proceedings and, where this is needed, also adds to the proceedings the owners of adjacent items.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is needed, the competent authority refers the application for the building permit:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg7p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for approval to the authority in whom the law vests competencies that are related to the subject matter of the application for the permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para42lg7p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for an opinion to the authority or person whose rights or interests may be affected by the construction work or building work envisaged in the application.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg8">
							<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where, in the course of referral for approvals and opinions, observations are filed concerning the application for the building permit, the competent authority takes appropriate consideration of these observations or states the reasons for not taking them into consideration. The building permit is issued electronically in the Register of Construction Works.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para42lg9">
							<loigeNr>9</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(9)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the authority whose approval or the person or authority whose opinion is requested has not, within ten days from receiving the application for the building permit, refused to give the approval or opinion or applied for an extension of that time limit, the application is deemed to have been tacitly approved by the authority, or the person or authority is deemed to have declined to express an opinion regarding the application, unless otherwise provided by law.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para43">
						<paragrahvNr>43</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 43.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Notice of commencement of building work and notice of complete demolition of a construction work</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para43lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A notice of commencement of building work is filed with the competent authority at least three days before building work commences to erect a construction work that is subject to the building permit requirement.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para43lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The notice of commencement of building work sets out particulars regarding the construction work, the time of commencement of building work, the name, contact information, personal identification code (in the absence of a such a code, the date of birth) or registration number in the Commercial Register, or other relevant register, of the person performing owner oversight and of the person performing building work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para43lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A notice of demolition of a construction work that was subject to the building permit or building notice requirement is filed with the competent authority at least three days after its demolition.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para43lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A notice of the demolition of a construction work sets out the cadastral code and the address of the land unit, its registration number in the Register of Construction Works and a statement regarding the complete demolition of the construction work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para43lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the requirements concerning the form of the notice of commencement of building work and of the notice of demolition of a construction work and the rules for their filing.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para44">
						<paragrahvNr>44</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 44.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Refusal to issue a building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para44lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority refuses to issue a building permit if:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the envisaged construction work does not conform to the detailed spatial plan, design specifications, a national or municipal designated spatial plan, the requirements established for construction works or for building work, or other public-law restrictions;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the building design documentation has not been created by a competent person or an expert assessment by a competent person has not been performed in respect of the building design documentation;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the building design documentation does not take into account the results of the site investigations conducted at the site of the construction work to be built or the required site investigations have not been performed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work or building work entails a permanent negative impact for the owner of the item of immovable property or the owners of adjacent items or other persons affected by the construction work or building work and it is not possible to sufficiently reduce or alleviate that impact;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the building design documentation does not conform to the requirements established for building design documentation;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the authority mentioned in clause 1 of subsection 7 of § 42 of this Code has – in a situation where where this was justified – refused to approve the application for the building permit;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the competent authority has initiated proceedings to repeal the detailed spatial plan that serves as the basis for the building design documentation;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the competent authority has initiated proceedings to revoke the design specifications that serve as the basis for the building design documentation;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a temporary ban on building work has been established with regard to the item of immovable property in respect of which the building permit is applied for;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p10">
								<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work or building work entails a significant environmental impact that cannot be sufficiently avoided or alleviated;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p10b1">
								<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work of building work creates a danger to national security or to a national defence object and the danger cannot be avoided or averted;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p10b2">
								<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="2">10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10<sup>2</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a building permit has been issued, or building permit proceedings are ongoing, for the same site and the simultaneous realisation of both permits is not possible;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p11">
								<alampunktNr>11</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[11)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the demolition of the construction work is contrary to a significant public interest;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para44lg1p12">
								<alampunktNr>12</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[12)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>in applying for the building permit, knowingly false information has been filed that has an impact on the decision on issuing the building permit.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para45">
						<paragrahvNr>45</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 45.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Validity period of building permits</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para45lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A building permit is valid for five years. When building work has commenced, the building permit remains valid for up to seven years from the time it became valid. Where this is justified, a longer validity period may be prescribed or the validity period may be varied in accordance with rules provided by legislation.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para45lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The date of commencement of building work is deemed to be the first day on which work corresponding to the building design documentation is performed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para46">
						<paragrahvNr>46</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 46.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Revocation of a building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para46lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority revokes a building permit where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para46lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the building design documentation that served as the basis for the application for building permit has been amended in a way that significantly changes important specifications of the construction work such as fire safety, energy performance, purpose of use, loads affecting the construction work or other important technical parameters stated in the permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para46lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>in applying for the permit, knowingly false information has been filed that had a significant impact on the decision on issuing the permit.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para46lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may revoke a building permit where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para46lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the holder of the permit or the owner of the item of immovable property has applied for the revocation, except where other persons have a legitimate interest in the validity of the permit, or</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para46lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work or building work does not conform to the building design documentation, the detailed spatial plan, the design specifications, a national or municipal designated spatial plan, or the requirements for construction works or for building work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para46lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>when issuing the permit, requirements emanating from legislation were not met and the construction works poses a danger to national security or to a national defence object and the danger cannot be avoided or averted - both of which conditions must be present simultaneously.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk5">
				<peatykkNr>5</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 5]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Use and Occupancy Notice and Use and Occupancy Permit</peatykkPealkiri>
				<jagu id="jg6">
					<jaguNr>1</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 1]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Use and Occupancy Notice</jaguPealkiri>
					<paragrahv id="para47">
						<paragrahvNr>47</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 47.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para47lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In situations falling under this section, the competent authority must be notified in advance of the use and occupancy of the construction work or of a change in its purpose of use.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para47lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A use and occupancy notice must be filed when the construction work is complete if the construction work or a part of the construction work is intended to be used and occupied and if, with regard to the construction work or the part of the construction work, the requirements for the use and occupancy of construction works have been met.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para47lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy notice is filed with the municipality, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para47lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy notice is filed with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority if the basis for building the construction work is provided by a national designated spatial plan or if building the construction work is related to building a construction work that conforms to such a plan.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para47lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The filing of a use and occupancy notice is required in respect of the construction works mentioned in Annex 2 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para47lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is warranted by the circumstances, the competent authority is authorised to require the filing of a use and occupancy notice in respect of a construction work that is not included in Annex 2 to this Code. When considering whether to require the filing of such a notice, the danger posed by the construction work and its impact on public space and on the rights of individuals is taken into account and a comparison is made with similar indications provided by Annex 2 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para47lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the building design documentation of a construction work subject to the use and occupancy permit requirement includes construction works whose use and occupancy is subject to the notification obligation, the fiilng of the application for the use and occupancy permit functions as the filing of the use and occupancy notice.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para47lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, requirements concerning the form of the use and occupancy notice and the rules for its filing.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para48">
						<paragrahvNr>48</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 48.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Filing a use and occupancy notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para48lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority is notified of the use and occupancy of a construction work electronically via the Register of Construction Works. Where it is not possible to make the notification via the Register, a use and occupancy notice is filed with the competent authority, who enters the corresponding information in the Register.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para48lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy notice must be filed at least ten days before commencement of the use and occupancy of the construction work or the change of its purpose of use. If, within ten days from the filing of the use and occupancy notice, the competent authority does not inform the person who filed the notice of the need for further verification of the information presented in the notice, the use and occupancy of the construction work may commence or the purpose of use of the construction work may be changed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para48lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy notice states:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the name, contact information and signature of the person filing the notice and the date of the filing;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the particulars and cadastral code of the item of immovable property on which the construction work is situated;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the aim of filing the use and occupancy notice, including a description of the construction work, its purpose of use and the type of building work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg3p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where the notice concerns a temporary construction work, the period time envisaged for the use of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg3p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where required, the energy performance certificate;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg3p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the particulars of the builder.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para48lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is mentioned in Annex 2 to this Code, the use and occupancy notice must be accompanied by the building design documentation according to which the construction work was built.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para48lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is needed, the competent authority verifies whether in relation to the use and occupancy of the construction work or the change in its purpose of use as stated in the use and occupancy notice, it is necessary:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg5p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to bring the construction work into conformity with the requirements;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg5p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to obtain the approval of the competent authority for the use and occupancy of the construction work or for the change in its purpose of use;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para48lg5p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to add the owner of the item of immovable property or the owners of adjacent items to the proceedings.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para48lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the grounds provided by subsection 5 of this section are present, the procedure established in relation to use and occupancy permits is observed, including the time limit of that procedure and the grounds for refusal to issue a use and occupancy permit. The requirements specified as a result of the verification are issued by the competent authority as an administrative decision.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para49">
						<paragrahvNr>49</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 49.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy of a construction work on the basis of a use and occupancy notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para49lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>On the basis of a use an occupancy notice, the construction work may be used and occupied indefinitely, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
				<jagu id="jg7">
					<jaguNr>2</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 2]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Use and Occupancy Permit</jaguPealkiri>
					<paragrahv id="para50">
						<paragrahvNr>50</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 50.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para50lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy permit is issued if the building work performed on the completed construction work conforms to the building permit and it is possible to use and occupy the construction work in compliance with the requirements and in accordance with its purpose of use. The permit is required in respect of construction works described in Annex 2 to this Code and in the event of a change in their purpose of use.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para50lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is warranted by the circumstances, the competent authority is authorised to issue a use and occupancy permit or to demand that a use and occupancy permit be issued in respect of a construction work not included in Annex 2 to this Code. When considering whether to issue the use and occupancy permit, the danger posed by the construction work and its impact on public space and on the rights of individuals is taken into account and a comparison is made with the similar indications provided by Annex 2 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para50lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy permit determines the purpose of use of the construction work or changes it.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para50lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the change in the purpose of use of the construction work does not entail any operations that are listed in Annex 1 to this Code as subject to the notice or permit requirement, that change in the purpose of use is subject to the column concerning changes in the purpose of use as established in Annex 2 to this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para50lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A use and occupancy permit may be issued in respect of a part of the construction work if that part is complete and the requirements established in legislation - first and foremost, the requirement that it is possible to use the construction work safely - have been complied with.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para50lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para50lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para50lg7p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the list of the purposes of use of construction works;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para50lg7p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the requirements for construction works arising from their purpose of use.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para51">
						<paragrahvNr>51</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 51.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Authority competent to issue the use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para51lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy permit is issued by the municipality, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para51lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the application for a use and occupancy permit includes construction works which were built on the basis of a national designated spatial plan or whose building was related to building a construction work that was in conformity with such a plan, the use and occupancy permit is issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, unless otherwise provided by law.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para51lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the application for a use and occupancy permit includes construction works in respect of which the issuing of the use and occupancy permit is in the competence of the state and of the municipality, the corresponding use and occupancy permit is issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para51lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If the application for a use and occupancy permit includes construction works in respect of which the issuing of the use and occupancy permit is in the competency of several government agencies, the corresponding use and occupancy permit is issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority, unless otherwise provided by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para52">
						<paragrahvNr>52</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 52.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Application for a use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para52lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a use and occupancy permit and related documents are filed with the competent authority electronically via the Register of Construction Works. Where it is not possible to file these documents via the Register, they are filed with the competent authority who enters the information in the Register.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para52lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a use and occupancy permit states:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the applicant's name, contact information and signature, and the date of the filing;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the manner of delivery of the use and occupancy permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the particulars and cadastral code of the item of immovable property on which building work is to be performed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the aim of applying for the permit, including the description and purpose of use of the completed construction work and the type of building work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where a temporary construction work is to be used, the period of use applied for;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>in situations provided for by legislation, maintenance instructions;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the particulars of the person who built the construction work and, where relevant, the particulars of the person who created the building design documentation and, where the conformity of the building design documentation to the requirements was verified by a competent person who is independent of the person who created the building design documentation, also the particulars of that competent person;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where required, the energy performance certificate;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>in situations provided for by legislation, proof of the construction work having being audited;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p10">
								<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>building documentation, except where the scope of the application for a use and occupancy permit is limited to changing the purpose of use of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para52lg2p11">
								<alampunktNr>11</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[11)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>information regarding payment of the statutory fee.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para52lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a use and occupancy permit must be accompanied by the building design documentation according to which the construction work was built. The filing of the building design documentation is not required if the scope of the application is limited to changing the purpose of use of the construction work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para52lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where, after the issuing of the building permit, an expert assessment has been conducted to verify whether the building design documentation meets the requirements, the expert assessment report is filed together with the application for the use and occupancy permit.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para52lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the application for a use and occupancy permit, the rules for its filing and the requirements concerning its form.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para53">
						<paragrahvNr>53</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 53.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Checking the application for a use and occupancy permit and refusing to consider the application</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para53lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When the competent authority receives an application for a use and occupancy permit, it verifies the conformity of the application to the requirements. Where it is manifest that the issuing of the use and occupancy permit is impossible, the competent authority dismisses the application and returns it, stating the reasons for dismissal. The impossibility of issuing the use and occupancy permit is manifest, first and foremost, where the building of the construction work required a building notice or building permit and the notice or permit does not exist.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para54">
						<paragrahvNr>54</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 54.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Procedure for issuing use and occupancy permits</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para54lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy permit is issued if the construction work conforms to the requirements established by legislation, i.e., above all to the requirements for construction works, and conforms to the building permit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para54lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority decides on the need to initiate the assessment of environmental impact above all, if the change in the purpose of use of the construction work may entail a significant environmental impact that has not been assessed before.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para54lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>By way of ancillary requirements, the use and occupancy permit may, above all, stipulate the following:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where warranted by the circumstances, the validity period of the permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg3p1b1">
								<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the validity period of the permit in relation to the time limit for demolishing the construction work and, where this is needed, with requirements concerning the post-demolition situation - where the ground for setting the time limit for demolition emanates from a legislative instrument or from a spatial plan or where the time limit emanates from an ancillary requirement of the building permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the validity period of the permit as related to the time limit for the demolition of a temporary construction work, which may not exceed five years since the issuing of the permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where the permit is issued in respect of a part of the construction work, the ancillary requirement to apply, within a specified time limit, for a use and occupancy permit for the entire construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg3p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the conduct of an expert assessment of the building design documentation, including the time limit for conducting the assessment;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg3p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the need to commission an opinion from a competent person to verify the compliance of the construction work with the requirements;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg3p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the requirement to perform an audit.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para54lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority issues the use and occupancy permit within 30 days from the date of filing of the application. The competent authority sets a time limit of up to ten days for the giving of approvals or opinions.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para54lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the application is not filed by the owner of the item of immovable property named in the application, the competent authority adds that owner to the proceedings and, where this is needed, also adds to the proceedings the owners of adjacent items.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para54lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is needed, the competent authority refers the application for the use and occupancy permit:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg6p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for approval to the authority in whom the law vests competencies that are related to the subject matter of the application for the permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para54lg6p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for an opinion to the authority or person whose rights or interests may be affected by the construction work.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para54lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where, in the course of referral fo approvals and opinions, observations are filed concerning the application for the use and occupancy permit, the competent authority takes appropriate consideration of these observations or states the reasons for not taking them into consideration. The use and occupancy permit is issued electronically in the Register of Construction Works.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para54lg8">
							<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the authority whose approval or the person or authority whose opinion is requested has not, within ten days from receiving the application for the use and occupancy permit, refused to give the approval or opinion or applied for an extension of that time limit, the application is deemed to have been tacitly approved by the authority, or the person or authority is deemed to have declined to express an opinion regarding the application, unless otherwise provided by law.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para55">
						<paragrahvNr>55</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 55.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Refusal to issue a use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para55lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority refuses to issue the use and occupancy permit where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work does not conform to the requirements;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work poses a danger as a result of the change in its purpose of use;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work does not conform to the building permit, to the national or municipal designated spatial plan or detailed spatial plan currently in effect, including the operational plan for implementation of the detailed spatial plan, or to the design specifications;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the competent authority has initiated proceedings to revoke the building permit that served as the basis for the building of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>due to changes in the building design documentation or changes made in the course of building work, the building design documentation filed with the application for a use and occupancy permit differs significantly from the building design documentation filed with the application for the building permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the building design documentation does not conform to the requirements established for the building design documentation that served as the basis for the building work and, due to this, the completed construction work poses a danger;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the audit has not been performed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the authority mentioned in clause 1 of subsection 6 of § 54 of this Code has, in a situation where this was justified, refused to approve the application for the use and occupancy permit;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the use and occupancy of the construction work entails a significant environmental impact that cannot be sufficiently avoided or alleviated;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p9b1">
								<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work does not correspond to the approval issued under subsection 3 of § 120 of this Code and its use and occupancy poses a danger to national security and the danger cannot be avoided or averted – both of which conditions must be present simultaneously, or</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para55lg1p10">
								<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>in applying for the use and occupancy permit, knowingly false information has been filed that had a material impact on the decision to issue the use and occupancy permit.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para56">
						<paragrahvNr>56</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 56.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Validity period of use and occupancy permits</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para56lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A use and occupancy permit is granted for an unspecified period, unless stipulated otherwise in the permit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para57">
						<paragrahvNr>57</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 57.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Revocation of a use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para57lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority revokes the use and occupancy permit where, when applying for the permit, knowingly false information has been filed that had a significant impact on the decision to issue the permit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para57lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may revoke a use and occupancy permit where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para57lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the holder of the permit or the owner of the item of immovable property has applied for the revocation, except where other persons have a legitimate interest in the validity of the permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para57lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the audit has not been performed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para57lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work or its use does not conform to the permit or to the requirements established for the construction work.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk6">
				<peatykkNr>6</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 6]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Register of Construction Works</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para58">
					<paragrahvNr>58</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 58.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Register of Construction Works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para58lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The purpose of keeping the Register of Construction Works is to ensure the presence of appropriate datasets for the purposes of proceedings related to construction works – including performance of regulatory enforcement – and for the setting, and implementation, of priorities in relation to construction works.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para58lg1b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Register of Construction Works is the single information point within the meaning of paragraph 1 of Article 6 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1309 of the European Parliament and of the Council of 29 April 2024 on measures to reduce the cost of deploying gigabit electronic communications networks, amending Regulation (EU) 2015/2120 and repealing Directive 2014/61/EU (Gigabit Infrastructure Act) (OJ L, 2024/1309, 08.05.2024).<reavahetus/>[RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para58lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The constitutive regulations of the Register of Construction Works are enacted by the Government of the Republic by means of a regulation that makes provision for:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para58lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>data providers and the data to be received from them;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para58lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>specific datasets;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para58lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the tasks of the controller and the processor;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para58lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the rules governing access to data;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para58lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>specific time limits of data retention;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para58lg2p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>other organisational matters.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para59">
					<paragrahvNr>59</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 59.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Controller and processor of the data in the Register of Construction Works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para59lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The controller of the data in the Register of Construction Works is the Ministry of Climate.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062023001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2023-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para59lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The processors of the data in the Register of Construction Works are designated in the Constitutive Regulations of the Register.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para60">
					<paragrahvNr>60</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 60.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Information recorded in the Register of Construction Works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para60lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Regular information recorded in the Register of Construction Works consists of:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>particulars of the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>particulars of the location of the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>building documentation;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>particulars of the building work performed;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>general data regarding the owner of a construction work that represents movable property;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>information on engineering investigations;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the particulars of any audits of the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>maintenance instructions for the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p9">
							<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>general data of persons connected with the construction work or the building work performed;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026];</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p10">
							<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>information concerning the applications, design specifications, notices, permits and compliance notices linked to the construction work or the building work performed;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p11">
							<alampunktNr>11</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[11)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>particulars of any regulatory enforcement action;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p12">
							<alampunktNr>12</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[12)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>particulars of the energy performance certificate;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p13">
							<alampunktNr>13</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[13)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>particulars of the physical infrastructure of the network operator or owner in accordance with paragraph 1 of Article 6 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1309;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para60lg1p14">
							<alampunktNr>14</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[14)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>where this is needed, other information related to the construction work or to the building work performed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para60lg1b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>While construction works that form a functional unit may be dealt with jointly for the purposes of notice and permit procedures provided by this Code, they are recorded separately in the Register of Construction Works.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para60lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Constitutive Regulations of the Register of Construction Works may, in relation to the purpose of use of construction works, specify the definition of the particulars or information set out in subsection 1 of this section and provide special rules to govern the entry of those particulars or that information in the Register.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para60lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The information in the Register of Construction Works is disseminated through the website of the Register. The information in the Register is made available via the X-road interface.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para60lg3b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The name, personal identification number, date of birth and contact particulars of natural persons connected to the construction work or building work are made public in the Register of Construction Works – including in documents recorded in the register that prove that the construction work, building work or use and occupancy of the construction work comply with the requirements – strictly where that information is required to ensure compliance with, and verification of, the requirements related to the construction work or to building work, and the conduct of the related proceedings.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para60lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Access via the website of the Register of Construction Works and the X-road interface is provided to the entirety of the particulars and information in the Register, with the exception of archived information of the Register of Buildings, the particulars of compliance notices that have been complied with and the particulars of construction works that have been removed from the Register.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para60lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by means of a regulation, requirements concerning the form of the notice of particulars to be filed with the Register of Construction Works and the rules for its filing.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para60lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The information in the Register of Construction Works is retained for an unspecified period. Constitutive regulations of the register may make provision for shorter periods of rentention.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-12-04</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>104122024001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2025-01-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61">
					<paragrahvNr>61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Significance of information stored in the Register of Construction Works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para61lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The information stored in the Register of Construction Works has informational and statistical significance.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para61lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Applications, design specifications, notices, superficies licences, building permits, use and occupancy permits, compliance notices and any decisions provided for by subsections 4 and 5 of § 822 of this Code have legal significance.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk7">
				<peatykkNr ylaIndeks="1">6</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 6<sup>1</sup>]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Facilitation of Deployment of High-Speed Electronic Communications Networks</peatykkPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				<paragrahv id="para61b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b2">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="2">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>2</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Definitions</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b3">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="3">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>3</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Exchange of information and determining the area of interest</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b4">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="4">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>4</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Access to data concerning physical infrastructure</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b5">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="5">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>5</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Access to physical infrastructure</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b6">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="6">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>6</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Access to information concerning planned building work</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b7">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="7">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>7</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Joint performance of building work</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b8">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="8">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>8</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>In-building physical infrastructure</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.02.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b9">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="9">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>9</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Access to in-building physical infrastructure</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b10">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="10">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>10</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Resolution of disputes before the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b11">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="11">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>11</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Obligation to provide information to the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para61b12">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="12">61</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 61<sup>12</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Right of access to a construction work owned by the state or by the municipality</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 25.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 12.05.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
		</osa>
		<osa id="o2">
			<osaNr>2</osaNr>
			<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Part 2]]></kuvatavNr>
			<osaPealkiri>SPECIAL CONSTRUCTION WORKS AND SPECIAL REQUIREMENTS</osaPealkiri>
			<peatykk id="ptk8">
				<peatykkNr>7</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 7]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Energy Performance of Buildings</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para62">
					<paragrahvNr>62</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 62.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para62lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The requirements established in this Chapter apply to buildings that use energy to control indoor climate and the quality of indoor air, including to maintain, increase or reduce indoor temperature.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para62lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The requirements established in this Chapter do not apply to the following buildings:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para62lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>buildings that, according to the relevant comprehensive spatial plan or detailed spatial plan, are situated within a built-up area of cultural and historical value or have been recognised as a valuable monument, or buildings which, under the Heritage Conservation Act, have been designated as monuments, are situated in a heritage conservation area or included in the UNESCO World Heritage List and in which compliance with the minimum requirements for energy performance would significantly alter the building's nature or appearance;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para62lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>buildings that are mainly used as places of worship or for religious activities;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para62lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>temporary buildings whose useful life is two years or less, industrial sites, workshops and non-residential agricultural buildings with low energy demand;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para62lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>residential buildings which are either intended to be used during less than four months of the year or have an alternatively limited period of annual use and whose expected energy consumption is less than 25 per cent of the energy consumption corresponding to year-round use;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para62lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>buildings whose enclosed net floor area does not exceed 50 m2.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para63">
					<paragrahvNr>63</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 63.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Definitions</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para63lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Energy performance of a building’ means the calculated or measured amount of energy needed to meet the energy demand associated with the typical use of the building, which includes, inter alia, energy used for heating, cooling, ventilation, the heating of water and lighting.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para63lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Minimum requirements for energy performance’ means the ceiling values of the total energy consumption of existing or new buildings, which are based on the purpose of use of the buildings and which take into account technical parameters, the requirements established for utility systems with a significant impact on the building’s energy performance or the requirements for introducing the use of renewable energy in buildings. Minimum requirements for energy performance may also include requirements for the building’s other utility systems if the operation of those systems causes the building’s energy demand to increase significantly.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para63lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<muutmismarge>
							<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para63lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Renovation is deemed to be major where the costs of modification of the building's envelope elements and the modification or replacement of the building's loadbearing or stiffening elements, or of modification of the building's outer envelope and the building's utility systems or parts thereof, or of the complete replacement of a utility system, exceed one quarter of the average building cost of a building that is equivalent to the building that is being renovated.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para63lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may make regulations to establish the rules for assessing average building cost.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para64">
					<paragrahvNr>64</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 64.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for the energy performance of buildings</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para64lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The building's outer envelope and utility systems with a significant impact on the building's energy performance must ensure that the total energy consumption of the building corresponds to the climatic conditions of its location and to the purpose of its use.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para64lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Measures must be taken to improve the energy performance of the building, taking into consideration the following requirements:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para64lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the energy performance may not be achieved in a manner that would adversely affect the building's indoor climate and the conditions of the building's use;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para64lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>different options must be weighed and cost-effective solutions must be preferred;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para64lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>when renovating a utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance, the optimum performance of such a system must be ensured.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para64lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A prerequisite for the optimum performance of a utility system is the appropriate choice of the system and of the equipment, their appropriate installation, setup and check and, where this is needed, the employment of a smart measuring system.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para64lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The energy audit is performed in order to obtain requisite knowledge concerning the energy consumption profile of a building or group of buildings, of an industrial or commercial process or installation or of specific services. The energy audit identifies cost-effective energy saving opportunities and quantifies the corresponding savings; an audit report is drawn up based on its results.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para64lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, requirements for the energy audits of buildings and for the methodology of calculating the energy performance of buildings.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para65">
					<paragrahvNr>65</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 65.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Minimum requirements for energy performance</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para65lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Any new building that is being built or any existing building that is undergoing major renovation must conform to the minimum requirements for energy performance after the completion of the building or renovation work. If the building work was performed on the basis of a building permit, the construction work must conform to the minimum requirements for energy performance that were in effect at the time the permit was issued.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The building's outer envelope and utility systems with a significant impact on the building's energy performance must be designed and built such that approaching them as an integral whole would allow for conformity to the minimum requirements for energy performance.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the minimum requirements for energy performance, including the requirements for utility systems with a significant impact on the building's energy performance, and the requirements for introducing the use of renewable energy in buildings. The minimum requirements for energy performance are reviewed at least once every five years. When reviewing the minimum requirements for energy performance, technical progress is taken into account.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para65b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">65</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 65<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Electric car charging infrastructure</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para65b1lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Electric car charging infrastructure’ means cabling infrastructure or a charging point or a combination of cabling infrastructure and a charging point.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b1lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Electric car cabling infrastructure’ means a cable protection conduit through which it is possible to run an electrical cable in order to install a charging point.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b1lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Electric car charging point’ means an interface of the charging infrastructure by means of which it is possible to charge one electric car at a time or to change the battery of one electric car at a time.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b1lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When erecting a building for the servicing of which more than ten parking spaces are prescribed, the following are to be installed:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para65b1lg4p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>cabling infrastructure for each parking space, if the building is a residential one,</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para65b1lg4p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>cabling infrastructure at least for each fifth parking space and an electric car charging point at least for one parking space, if the building is a non-residential one.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b1lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When electric car charging infrastructure is to be installed in a building with several purposes of use of which at least one is a residential use or at least one is a non-residential use, the installation is subject either to the requirements applicable to residential or to non-residential buildings, according to the principal use recorded in respect of the building in the Register of Construction Works.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b1lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When undertaking a major renovation of a building for the servicing of which more than ten parking spaces are prescribed, the requirements provided for by subsections 4 and 5 of this section are to be complied with if the work to be carried out as part of such renovation also extends to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para65b1lg6p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the building’s car park or</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para65b1lg6p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the electrical system of the building or of the car park.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b1lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If more than 20 parking spaces are prescribed for the servicing of a non-residential building, an electric car charging point must be installed at least for one such space.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para65b2">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="2">65</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 65<sup>2</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Renovation support measure</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para65b2lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Renovation support measures intended for improving the energy performance of buildings are linked to envisaged or achieved energy savings.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b2lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>To determine the energy saving, the situation prior to renovation is compared to the envisaged or realised solution, using at least one of the following indicators:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para65b2lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the energy performance indicator determined based on typical use data;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para65b2lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the value of weighted specific energy consumption determined based on actual consumption data;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para65b2lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>estimated change in energy consumption set out in the relevant energy audit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b2lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If, to determine energy savings, a renovation support measure employs an indicator other than those provided for by subsection 2 of this section, the measure must include a description of the envisaged indicator and the energy savings determined using that indicator must be comparable and verifiable.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para65b2lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where equipment or material is installed by a person who meets the relevant qualification requirements, to determine the corresponding energy saving the energy performance indicator of existing equipment or material may be compared to that of the equipment or material that is being installed.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para66">
					<paragrahvNr>66</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 66.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Energy performance certificate</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para66lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Conformity to the minimum requirements for energy performance is proved by means of the energy performance certificate. An energy performance certificate provides information on the rated energy demand or the actual energy consumption of a building that already exists or that is being designed.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para66lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A list of recommendations for improving the energy performance of the building is annexed to the energy performance certificate, except where there is no reasonable possibility for making the corresponding improvements.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para66lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>An energy performance certificate issued in respect of the rated energy demand is valid for two years after the completion of the building. An energy performance certificate issued in respect of actual energy consumption is valid for ten years. A subsequently issued energy performance certificate revokes the energy performance certificate issued previously in respect of the same building or part of the building.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para66lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If the building lacks a common heating system, a separate energy performance certificate may be issued in respect of a part of that building that can be used separately.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para66lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The energy performance certificate is issued by a competent person who is a member of the relevant profession. The person who issues the energy performance certificate enters the particulars of that certificate electronically in the Register of Construction Works. The particulars of the energy performance certificate issued in respect of a building that is being designed are entered in the Register at the latest at the time of the filing of the use and occupancy notice or of the application for a use and occupancy permit.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para66lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the requirements for energy performance certificates and for the issuing of such certificates.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para67">
					<paragrahvNr>67</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 67.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Energy performance certificate when ownership of a building is transferred or the right to use and occupy the building is assigned for a fee</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para67lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In order to allow a person interested in buying a building or acquiring the right to use and occupy a building to make an informed choice, the advertisement regarding the transfer of ownership in the building or part of the building for a fee or regarding assignment of the right to use and occupy the building – or a part of the building that can be used separately – for a fee must include the particulars of the energy certificate, including the energy performance indicator or the weighted specific energy use and the corresponding class.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para67lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A person interested in buying a building or acquiring the right to use and occupy a building or a part of the building that can be used separately must be allowed to inspect the energy performance certificate. The energy performance certificate or a copy of the certificate is delivered upon the execution of the corresponding agreement to the person who acquires ownership of or the right to use and occupy the building or a part of the building that can be used separately. This requirement is deemed to have been met if it is possible to view the energy performance certificate in the Register of Construction Works.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para68">
					<paragrahvNr>68</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 68.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Displaying the energy performance certificate</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para68lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The energy performance certificate must be displayed in a prominent place clearly visible to the public in any building in which:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para68lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the enclosed net floor area exceeds 500 square metres and which is visited by crowds of people;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para68lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a state or municipal authority or any other public-law authority occupies an enclosed net floor area that exceeds 250 square metres and that is often visited by people.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para68lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may make regulations to establish a list of the types of building which are linked to the gathering of crowds and in relation to which the presence of an energy performance certificate is required.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para68lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The energy performance certificate must be displayed in a prominent place clearly visible to the public in any building that is covered by the list of the types of building established under subsection 2 of this section.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para69">
					<paragrahvNr>69</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 69.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Energy performance of heating and cooling systems</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<muutmismarge>
						<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
						<avaldamismarge>
							<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
							<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
							<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
							<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
						</avaldamismarge>
						<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
					</muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para69b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">69</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 69<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Utility system with a significant impact on the building’s energy performance</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para69b1lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Utility system with a significant impact on the building’s energy performance’ means:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para69b1lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a heating system or a household water heating system together with the source of heat;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b1lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a cooling system;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b1lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>an automation and control system (below, <i>automation system</i>);</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b1lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a ventilation system;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b1lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a lighting system;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b1lg1p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a system producing thermal energy or electricity locally.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b1lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Automation system’ means a system that comprises all products, software and services that support the energy-efficient, sustainable and safe operation of a building’s utility systems. An automation system must facilitate control of such systems, at the same time allowing for them to be controlled manually.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para69b2">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="2">69</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 69<sup>2</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Installation of a utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para69b2lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Any utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance, including any manually built system operating on solid fuel, must be installed or constructed in accordance with the requirements. To be deemed in accordance with the requirements, installation or construction needs to have observed the good practice of the relevant field, the relevant standard or the installation instructions.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b2lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The settings of a utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance must be adjusted to an optimal level, considering the typical use of the building or room to be served by that system.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b2lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Together with a utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance, which allows for automated regulation, a central automation system that makes it possible to constantly control and monitor the building's utility systems must be installed.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b2lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where, in connection with the installation of a heating source, replacement of the heating system and the household water heating system, or the existing heating source, is performed, such a heating source’s seasonal coefficient of performance, which has been reduced to primary energy terms and which is determined following the requirements of Directive 2009/125/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council establishing a framework for the setting of eco-design requirements for energy-related products (OJ L 285, 31.10.2009, pp. 10−35), must be at least 80 per cent.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b2lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The limit value of the seasonal coefficient of performance provided for by subsection 4 of this section does not apply where the unadjusted payback period of the heating source to be installed is longer than 20 years. When determining the unadjusted payback period, the installation cost of the equipment and of the utility system connected to that equipment, as well as the total of the energy, maintenance and operating costs for a 20-year period, are taken into account.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b2lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When replacing the heating source of a heating system, the system is equipped with self-regulation equipment, provided this is technically feasible.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b2lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where this is technically feasible and economically justified, the heating system of a building to be erected is furnished with self-regulation equipment that controls temperature in each room to be heated or in the area to be heated in each of the building's parts.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para69b3">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="3">69</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 69<sup>3</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Assessment of the energy performance of a utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para69b3lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When a utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance is installed, replaced or remodelled, the energy performance of the installed, replacement or remodelled system is assessed. The assessor enters the particulars of the assessment in the Register of Construction Works electronically.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b3lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>To assess the energy performance of an existing building's heating or cooling system whose rated capacity exceeds 70 kilowatts and which may or may not include a ventilation system, an inspection of the building's utility system is performed. In the course of the inspection, the effectiveness and capacity of the heating source or the cooling equipment or, where the system is a combined one, also of the ventilation unit, is assessed based on the building's heating or cooling need. The assessor enters the particulars of the assessment in the Register of Construction Works electronically.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b3lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When filing the application for a use and occupancy permit, or a use and occupancy notice, the assessment of the energy performance of a heating or cooling system whose rated capacity exceeds 70 kilowatts is annexed to such an application or such a notice.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b3lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where, subsequently to an energy performance assessment under subsection 2 or subsection 3 of this section, the heating or cooling system, which may or may not include a ventilation system, has not been modified, or the building's heating or cooling need has not changed, the assessment is not repeated.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b3lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The assessment of the energy performance of the heating or cooling system under subsection 2 or subsection 3 of this section is not conducted where:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para69b3lg5p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>an energy efficiency agreement within the meaning of the Energy Sector Organisation Act has been concluded for improving the energy performance of the heating or cooling system, which may or may not include a ventilation system;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b3lg5p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>an automation system meeting the requirements provided for by subsection 2 of § 69<sup>4</sup> of this Code has been installed in the building.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b3lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by means of a regulation, the rules for assessing the energy performance of a utility system with a significant impact on the building’s energy performance, the list of particulars to be entered in the Register of Construction Works concerning the assessment and the rules concerning the filing of those particulars.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para69b4">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="4">69</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 69<sup>4</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Improving the energy performance of a heating or cooling system of a non-residential building</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para69b4lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>To improve the energy performance of a non-residential building’s actual or designed heating or cooling system whose rated capacity exceeds 290 kilowatts and which may or may not include a ventilation system, the building’s owner installs in it an automation system, provided this is technically feasible and economically justified. Information concerning the technical feasibility and economic justifiability of an automation system of an existing non-residential building is filed electronically in the Register of Construction Works and information concerning a designed non-residential building is annexed to the application for a use and occupancy permit or to the use and occupancy notice.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para69b4lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>An automation system installed in order to comply with the requirement provided for by subsection 1 of this section must:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para69b4lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>make it possible to constantly control and monitor the building's energy consumption and to collect and analyse the building's energy performance consumption data;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b4lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>make it possible to analyse the building's energy performance in a comparative manner so as to ascertain any reductions in the energy performance of the building's utility systems, in order to notify building's owner or the operator of the building's utility systems of possibilities for improving the energy performance;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b4lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>provide for data transmission between a utility system with a significant impact on the building's energy performance, which is connected to the building's automation system, and other equipment situated in the building;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para69b4lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>provide for interoperability between technical solutions, equipment and utility systems with a significant impact on the building's energy performance that belong to different manufacturers.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk9">
				<peatykkNr>8</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 8]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Construction Works – Protection Zone</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para70">
					<paragrahvNr>70</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 70.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Construction works – protection zone</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para70lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of a construction work is the land underneath and around the construction work within which the owner of the item of immovable property is obligated to tolerate the presence of a construction work belonging to another and within which the use of and operations on the item are restricted for the purposes of safety and of ensuring the functionality of such a construction work.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para70lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone, it is prohibited:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to endanger the construction work or any use of the construction work that follows established rules;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to build another construction work subject to the building permit requirement, including the removal or heaping of soil;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to obstruct access to the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to obstruct maintenance of the construction work, including the installation of signs to alert the observer to the location of the construction work that has a protection zone or to the danger posed by such a construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to obstruct removal of a threat presented by plant life or soil to a construction work that possesses a protection zone;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg2p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to pursue any other activities provided for by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para70lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The restrictions of the protection zone may be derogated from with the consent of the owner of the construction work that enjoys the protection zone, provided this does not reduce the safety of the construction work. The owner of such a construction work may not charge a fee for giving their consent or demand the establishment of additional restrictions that are not related to safety. The owner may not refuse to give their consent without valid reasons. The owner is entitled to demand that any person carrying out operations within the protection zone act under their immediate supervision.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para70lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner of a construction work that enjoys a protection zone provides information regarding the location of that construction work free of charge to the owner of the item of immovable property and to any lawful user of the immovable.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para70lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner of a construction work that enjoys a protection zone must:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg5p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>act in a manner that entails the least possible infringement of the rights of the owner of the item of immovable property;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg5p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>when exercising their rights, take into consideration the legitimate interests of the owner of the item of immovable property, including giving reasonable advance notice to the owner of the land of any building work or repair work before the commencement of such work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para70lg5p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>ensure the preservation of the item of immovable property in good condition during any maintenance work performed on the construction work that enjoys a protection zone and, once the maintenance work has been completed, restore the item to its former condition, except where restoration to such condition would contravene the restrictions of the protection zone.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para70lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>If several construction works that enjoy a protection zone are built on the same item of immovable property, the greatest possible spatial overlap of the protection zones and the least possible encumbrance of the item of immovable property must be preferred where this is possible. It is deemed possible that a construction work that enjoys a protection zone may be built in the protection zone of another construction work that enjoys a protection zone.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para70lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The information regarding the existence of a protection zone, its content and spatial extent is entered in the Land Cadastre. The information to be entered in the Land Cadastre is provided by the owner of the construction work that enjoys the protection zone. If, after the building of a new construction work or after changing the location of an already existing construction work the application for entering the information concerning the protection zone in the Land Cadastre has not been filed with the Land Cadastre within 30 days following the completion of the building of the construction work or following its relocation, the obligation to tolerate the construction work does not arise and the owner of the item of immovable property is entitled to demand the removal of the construction work from the item.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para70lg8">
						<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the extent of protection zones, their protection and marking out and the recommendations for carrying out operations within protection zones.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para71">
					<paragrahvNr>71</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 71.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Protection zone – public roads</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para71lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of a public road is the area of land occupied by and surrounding the road that allows for protection of the road, for the organisation of road maintenance, for safe traffic on the road and reduces the harmful impact that is produced by the road with respect to the environment and the hazard that the road represents for people. If the road is a public road, it has a protection zone.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para71lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The width of the protection zone of a highway that is part of the trans-European road network mentioned in subsection 9 of § 92 of this Code is 50 metres from the outer edge of the outermost lane on both sides of the highway. The width of the protection zone of other highways is 30 metres from the outer edge of the outermost lane on both sides of the road. <reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para71lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The width of the protection zone of a street is 10 metres from the outer edge of the outermost lane on both sides of the street. The width of the protection zone may be extended up to 50 metres where this is prescribed by the comprehensive spatial plan or detailed spatial plan.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para71lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner of the road may, where this is justified, reduce the width of the protection zone mentioned in subsections 2 and 3 of this section.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para72">
					<paragrahvNr>72</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 72.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Operations within the protection zone of a road</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para72lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone of a road, it is prohibited to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para72lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>install any lighting equipment, information or advertising device that disturbs traffic on the road;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para72lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>hold sports events and other public events;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para72lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>extract mineral resources and earth materials;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para72lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>store forest material and process timber;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para72lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>perform work that entails a change in the water regime;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para72lg1p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>erect a sales point of any other service counter – where the road is a highway that is part of the trans-Euroipean road network mentioned in subsection 9 of § 92 of this Code.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para72lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner of the item of immovable property to which the protection zone of the road extends is obligated to permit the removal of any flora, structure or construction work that restricts visibility and poses a traffic hazard. The owner must, in the protection zone of the road and for road maintenance purposes, allow the installation of temporary snow fences, the construction of snow walls and ditches to block drifting snow and must allow snow to be cleared to land outside the road area, provided these activities do not obstruct access to the property.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para72lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Detours may be constructed and built and another item of immovable property used for their maintenance only on contractual basis. In the event of an accident or natural disaster, conclusion of the contract is not required. The owner of the item must be paid compensation for any harm resulting from the temporary use of the item.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para72lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In areas where the creation of a detailed spatial plan is mandatory, buildings that are subject to the detailed spatial plan requirement may be built in the protection zone of the road if this is permitted in the detailed spatial plan or in the national or municipal designated spatial plan.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para73">
					<paragrahvNr>73</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 73.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Protection zone – railways</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para73lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of a railway includes the ground underneath the railway and extends to 30 metres from the axis of the track or, in multitrack railways and railway stations, from the axis of the outermost track.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para73lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone of a railway, it is prohibited to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para73lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>endanger rail traffic and obstruct visibility on the railway;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para73lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>construct land improvement systems, extract minerals and perform excavation work;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para73lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>carry out forest renewal cutting as well as perform any other work that changes the natural environment;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para73lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>produce and store flammable substances and explosives;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para73lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>store and install equipment and materials – where this jeopardises visibility in the protection zone;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para73lg2p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>build construction works.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para73lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para73lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Prior to providing the consent mentioned in subsection 3 of § 70 of this Code, the owner of the railway may, where this is justified, require the person requesting the consent to draw up a risk analysis or any other relevant analysis in order to assess the impact of the envisaged activity on the condition of the railway and on rail traffic.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para73lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where a swath of forest situated in the protection zone obstructs the visibility needed for ensuring the safety of railway traffic or where a swath situated within ten metres from the axes of the track is the source of a potential risk of fire and the owner of the item of immovable property does not file the notice of forest cutting operations or does not cut the swath, or where the visibility needed for ensuring the safety of railway traffic is obstructed or the source of the potential risk of fire is represented by other plants that do not qualify as woodland and the owner of the item does not clear these plants, the railway infrastructure manager or other owner or operator of the railway is authorised to arrange, in the railway protection zone and in order to ensure the safety of railway traffic, the cutting of the swath or the clearing of other plants. The railway infrastructure manager or other owner or possessor of the railway informs the owner of the item in advance of the corresponding operations and of the measures to be taken while performing them.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para74">
					<paragrahvNr>74</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 74.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Protection zone – public water supply or sewerage construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para74lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of a public water supply or sewerage construction work is the area of land that surrounds such a construction work and in that the use of an item of immovable property has been restricted in order to ensure the safety and protection of that construction work.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para74lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone of a public water supply or sewerage construction work, it is prohibited to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para74lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>store materials and carry out any blasting, drilling, excavation, pile ramming, mineral resource extraction, land raising, flooding or land drainage operations, and, near construction works, also any lifting operations;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para74lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>near a public water supply or sewerage construction work that is situated in a water body, perform any dredging operations or remove soil, dispose of solid substances, anchor water craft, or drag anchors, chains, logs, trawls or nets;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para74lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>plant trees.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para75">
					<paragrahvNr>75</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 75.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Protection zone – pressure equipment</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para75lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of pressure equipment is the land area which surrounds the pressure equipment that constitutes an independent construction work, and within which the use of the item of immovable property has been restricted in order to ensure the safety and protection of the pressure equipment.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para75lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone of pressure equipment, it is prohibited to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para75lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>store waste, chemicals or fertilisers;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para75lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>perform any blasting, drilling and excavation, as well as flooding, irrigation and land improvement operations, to store and move heavy objects and to arrange crossings of vehicles and to perform other work that may jeopardise the safety of the pressure equipment.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para76">
					<paragrahvNr>76</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 76.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Protection zone – gas installations</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para76lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of a gas installation is the land area which surrounds the gas installation that constitutes an independent construction work, and within which the use of the item of immovable property has been restricted in order to ensure the safety and protection of the gas installation.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para76lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone of a gas installation, it is prohibited to light fires and to grow trees. In the protection zone of a gas installation situated in a water body, it is prohibited to perform dredging operations, anchor water craft or navigate with sunk anchors, chains, logs, trawls or nets.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para77">
					<paragrahvNr>77</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 77.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Protection zone – electrical installations</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para77lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of an electrical installation is the land area which surrounds an electrical installation within the meaning of the Electricity Market Act that constitutes an independent construction work, and within which the use of the item of immovable property has been restricted in order to ensure the safety and protection of the electrical installation.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para77lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone of an electrical installation, it is prohibited:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para77lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to store waste, materials, substances and objects that endanger or obstruct access to the installation, to perform any kind of mining, loading, deepening, blasting and land improvement operations, to light fires, plant and cut trees;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para77lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to anchor water craft or navigate with sunk anchors, chains, logs, trawls or nets, to install traffic signs and buoys for water craft, and – in the protection zone of an electrical installation constructed as a submerged cable line – to harvest ice;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para77lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>– in the protection zone of overhead transmission lines – to drive machines and mechanisms whose total height above ground with or without cargo exceeds 4.5 metres;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para77lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>– in the protection zone of overhead transmission lines of high-voltage installations – to build wire or metal fences, to construct drinking sites for animals and to hold large-scale events;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para77lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>– in the protection zone of overhead transmission lines and of underground cable lines – to work with impact mechanisms, to level ground, to perform topsoil work at a level deeper than 0.3 metres below ground or at a level deeper than 0.45 metres in land subject to ploughing, and to store and move heavy objects.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para78">
					<paragrahvNr>78</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 78.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Protection zone – communications construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para78lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of a communications construction work that constitutes an independent construction work is the land area which surrounds it and within which the use of the item of immovable property has been restricted in order to ensure the safety and protection of the communications construction work. A communications construction work is deemed to mean such a construction work as defined in Chapter 9 of this Code.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para78lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the protection zone of a communications construction work, it is prohibited:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para78lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to perform any kind of mining, loading, deepening, blasting, flooding, irrigation and land improvement operations, to plant or cut trees, to remove tree stumps, to light fires, to use flammable materials and substances, to store waste, to obstruct access to the construction work and, by any actions, to cause corrosion of the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para78lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to climb a radio tower and to attach objects to a radio tower or to the fencing structures around the radio tower;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para78lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to perform deepening operations, to anchor water craft or navigate with sunk anchors, chains, logs, trawls or nets, to install traffic signs and buoys for water craft, and – in the protection zone of a communications construction work situated in a water body – to blast and harvest ice;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para78lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>– in the protection zone of a communications construction work constructed as an overhead line – to drive machines and mechanisms whose total height above ground with or without cargo exceeds 4.5 metres;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para78lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>– in the protection zone of an underground communications construction work – to work with impact mechanisms, to compact or level ground, to perform topsoil work at a level deeper than 0.3 metres below ground or at a level deeper than 0.45 metres in land subject to ploughing.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk10">
				<peatykkNr>9</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 9]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Installations and Communications Construction Works</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para79">
					<paragrahvNr>79</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 79.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application and single national digital entry point</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
					<loige id="para79lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The provisions in this Chapter apply to communications installations and construction works, including very high capacity communication networks.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para79lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Ministry of Justice and Digital Affairs serves as the single national entry point mentioned in paragraph 3 of Article 12 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1309 of the European Parliament and of the Council.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para80">
					<paragrahvNr>80</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 80.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Installations and communications construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para80lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>For the purposes of this Code, ‘installation’ means equipment within the meaning of the Equipment Safety Act that is permanently installed in a construction work or that constitutes an independent construction work. Installations are primarily:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para80lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>electrical installations;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para80lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>storage tanks and piping, including gas installations;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para80lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>lifts;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para80lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>cableways.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para80lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Communications construction work’ means a line or a line civil engineering work, including very high capacity communication network, within the meaning of the Electronic Communication Act.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para80lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Lift’ means:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para80lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a lifting device which is permanently installed in a construction work to move between its different levels, whose lift height exceeds 2.5 metres and which is intended either exclusively for the transport of people or for the transport of people and objects or exclusively for the transport of objects, provided that people have unobstructed access to the platform or car and controls are located on the platform or in the car, or within the reach of persons on the platform or in the car;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para80lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a lifting device that moves along a fixed course as provided for by clause 1 of this subsection even if it does not move along rigid guides (for example, a scissor lift).</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para80lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The platform or car is the part of the lift that is used to lift or lower people or objects that are on it or in it.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para80lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The installer of a lift is the person who assumes responsibility for the design, manufacture, installation and placing on the market of the lift. The installer of a lift is its manufacturer within the meaning of the Product Conformity Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para80lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Solar energy equipment, heat pumps and energy storage, including storage of electricity and of thermal energy, as well as the means needed to connect such equipment, pumps and storage to the grid and for integrating renewable energy into heating and cooling networks, are deemed the building’s utility system provided they are required for the operation or use of the building, or to ensure its safety.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 18.03.2026, 1 – entry into force 28.03.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para81">
					<paragrahvNr>81</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 81.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for lifts and for the building of lifts</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para81lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The lift and its safety components must conform to the requirements arising from the Product Conformity Act and the conformity of the lift and its safety components to these requirements must be proved following applicable rules before the lift and its safety components are placed on the market and put into commission.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para81lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Access to the engine assembly and related equipment of the lift or cableway must be obstructed. Access to the engine assembly and related equipment of the lift or cableway must only be possible for repair and maintenance purposes or in the case of danger.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para81lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The shaft of the lift may not contain cables, pipes and other equipment that is not required for the functioning of the lift. The room that contains the lift's engine assembly and related equipment may not contain equipment that is not required for the lift's operation if such equipment hinders maintenance and repair operations on the lift.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para81lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The installer of the lift and the person responsible for the building of the construction work must provide information to each other in matters pertaining to the installation of the lift and take the necessary measures to ensure the conformity of the installation to the requirements and the safety of use of the lift.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para82">
					<paragrahvNr>82</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 82.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for the marking out of communications construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para82lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The marking out of the location of a communications construction work that is being designed or built is specified in the building design documentation of the construction work and the owner of the item of immovable property is asked for an opinion in the matter.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the owner of the item of immovable property desires this or where the owner of the communications construction work deems this necessary, the location of a communications construction work in use is marked out with above-ground stakes or with warning signs.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Unauthorised removal, relocation or damaging of the markings of a communications construction work or reducing the visibility of the markings in any other manner is prohibited.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para82b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">82</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 82<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for very high capacity communication networks</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para82b1lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Requirements for the design and construction of communication networks are enacted by a regulation of the minister in charge of the policy sector.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b1lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Paragraphs 1, 2 and 3 of Article 10 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1309 of the European Parliament and of the Council are not applied in the case of the following buildings:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para82b1lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>buildings mentioned in clause 1 of subsection 2 of § 62 of this Code, whose nature or appearance would be altered by installation of very high capacity networks or elements thereof;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para82b1lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>buildings mentioned in clauses 2 and 3 of subsection 2 of § 62 of this Code;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para82b1lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>buildings with a surface projection area of up to 60 square metres;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para82b1lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>single-apartment residential buildings;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para82b1lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>construction works that serve national defence purposes, construction works of the security authorities or infrastructure at the national border.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 – entry into force 12.02.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b1lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Paragraphs 1, 4 and 5 of Article 3 and paragraphs 1, 3 and 5 of Article 4 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1309 of the European Parliament and of the Council are not applied in the case of the following types of physical infrastructure – and of particulars of such infrastructure – of public sector bodies:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para82b1lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>buildings mentioned in clause 1 of subsection 2 of § 62 of this Code, whose nature or appearance would be altered by installation of very high capacity networks or elements thereof;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b1lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>buildings mentioned in clause 2 of subsection 2 of § 62 of this Code;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b1lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>construction works that serve national defence purposes, construction works of the security authorities or infrastructure at the national border.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 – entry into force 12.05.2026]</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b1lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Paragraphs 2 and 4 of Article 5 and paragraph 1 of Article 6 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1309 of the European Parliament and of the Council are not applied when granting access to information concerning the planning of building work and to construction works whose construction does not require the filing of a building notice or the issue of a building permit, as well as to construction works that serve national defence purposes, to construction works of the security authorities and to infrastructure at the national border.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 – entry into force 12.05.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para82b2">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="2">82</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 82<sup>2</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Right to access construction works owned by the state or municipality</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para82b2lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A communications undertaking may file, by electronic means via the Register of Construction Works, an application to the state or municipality for access to a construction work owned by the state or municipality in order to install an active device of a mobile telephone network, including a base station and the antennae connected to it as well as a small-area wireless access point.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b2lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The state or municipality may only require the owner of the active device of the mobile telephone network to compensate the costs that arise in relation to installing the active device mentioned in subsection 1 of this section, to its continued use and to its removal.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b2lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The application mentioned in subsection 1 of this section must contain the following:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>contact particulars of the communications undertaking;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the location, including coordinates, for installation of the active device of the mobile telephone network;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>a technical drawing of the installation of the active device.</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b2lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The state or municipality decides the grant of access to install the active device of the mobile telephone network within two months following reception of the corresponding application. Decisions are made in the order the applications were filed.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b2lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The state or municipality may refuse access to install the active device of the mobile telephone network where:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg5p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the construction work is not suited, technically or because of its architecture, for installation of the active device;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg5p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>this endangers the life or health of humans;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg5p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the construction work is a building mentioned in clauses 1 and 2 of subsection 2 of § 62 of this Code;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg5p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>this represents a threat to national security;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg5p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the construction work does not have sufficient space for installation of the active device;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para82b2lg5p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the construction work is connected to the integrity and safety of the infrastructure required for provision of a vital service.</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para82b2lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The decisions made under subsections 4 and 5 of this section are presented electronically via the Register of Construction Works. The decisions made under subsections 4 and 5 of this section, with the exception of decisions made on the ground mentioned in clause 4 of subsection 5, are made public in the Register.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 – entry into force 12.05.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para83">
					<paragrahvNr>83</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 83.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para83lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are required:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para83lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>in relation to a communications construction work – with the exception of lines – for the creation of building design documentation concerning a new line civil engineering work;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para83lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for the construction of a new electrical installation that is subject to the building permit obligation and that traverses two or more items of immovable property or<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para83lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for increasing the nominal voltage of an existing electrical installation to 110 kilovolts or more.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para83lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are not issued if the building of the construction work mentioned in subsection 1 of this section is prescribed by a detailed spatial plan or a national or municipal designated spatial plan.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para84">
					<paragrahvNr>84</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 84.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Resolution of disputes arising in relation to communications construction works</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para84lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When resolving disputes arising in relation to communications construction works, the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority takes guidance from the provisions established in § 149 of Electronic Communications Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para84lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Disputes arising in relation to communications construction works must be resolved within six months.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para84lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the case of disputes relating to very high capacity communication networks, the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority serves as the national dispute settlement body within the meaning of Article 14 of Regulation (EU) 2024/1309 of the European Parliament and of the Council.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para84b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">84</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 84<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building permit for a thermal power station</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para84b1lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In relation to the building or remodelling of a thermal power station, the application for the building permit is filed together with an analysis that meets the requirements of § 10 of the Energy Sector Organisation Act of the costs and benefits of turning the thermal power station into an efficient cogeneration plant, if such an analysis is required under that section.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para84b1lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The building permit applied for in order to build or remodel a thermal power station is not granted if the building design documentation of the electrical installation of the thermal power station to be built or remodelled does not conform to a positive result of the analysis of costs and benefits mentioned in subsection 1 of this section.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2016-07-05</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>105072016003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2016-07-15</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para84b2">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="2">84</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 84<sup>2</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building notice for solar energy equipment with a capacity below 100 kilowatts</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para84b2lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where, in building notice proceedings for the construction – as a civil engineering work or as a utility system – of solar energy equipment with a capacity below 100 kilowatts, the competent authority, having initiated the verification provided for by subsection 5 of § 36 of this Code, has not issued an administrative decision within the time-limit prescribed by subsection 6 of § 36, building work may commence.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 18.03.2026, 1 – entry into force 28.03.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para85">
					<paragrahvNr>85</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 85.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy notice and use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para85lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where, in order to begin using a construction work, a use and occupancy notice must be filed or a use and occupancy permit is required, and where the construction work or an installation in the construction work is subject to an audit or inspection requirement, the use and occupancy notice or the application for a use and occupancy permit must be accompanied by an opinion that results from a pre-use audit or from an inspection and that shows the construction work or installation to be in conformity with the requirements.</tavatekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>2</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130122020002</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para85lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk11">
				<peatykkNr>10</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 10]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Railway Civil Engineering Works</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para86">
					<paragrahvNr>86</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 86.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para86lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The provisions in this Chapter apply to railway civil engineering works.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para87">
					<paragrahvNr>87</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 87.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for use and maintenance</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para87lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In addition to the requirements arising from this Code, the use and maintenance of railway civil engineering works is subject to the requirements arising from the Railways Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-10-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130102020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-10-31</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para88">
					<paragrahvNr>88</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 88.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para88lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The creation of building design documentation concerning a railway civil engineering work that is subject to the building permit requirement and that is mentioned in Annex 1 to this Code Design requires corresponding design specifications, except where such a civil engineering work is to be demolished.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para88lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications for a railway civil engineering work are issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-10-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130102020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-10-31</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para88lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Approval for design specifications for a railway civil engineering work must be obtained from the municipality concerned.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-10-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130102020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-10-31</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para89">
					<paragrahvNr>89</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 89.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building notice and building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para89lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>To build a railway civil engineering work, a building notice is filed with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority or a building permit is issued by the Authority.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-10-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130102020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-10-31</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para90">
					<paragrahvNr>90</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 90.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy notice and use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para90lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In order to start using a railway civil engineering work, the use and occupancy notice is filed with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority who also issues the use and occupancy permit.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-10-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130102020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-10-31</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk12">
				<peatykkNr>11</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 11]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Roads</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para91">
					<paragrahvNr>91</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 91.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para91lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The requirements in this Chapter apply to public roads and to private roads accessible to the public. Of the requirements provided by this Chapter, only those of § 93 apply to forest roads.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para91lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The provisions on the Register of Construction Works may be applied to the building, design and maintenance of roads as well as to any related activities.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para92">
					<paragrahvNr>92</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 92.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Definitions</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para92lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Road’ means a civil engineering work that is intended for the movement or traffic of humans, vehicles or animals. Tunnels, bridges, overpasses and other civil engineering works used for traffic and required for the functioning of the road are regard as parts of the road.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Highway’ means a road that is situated outside cities, towns or small towns and that is intended for vehicle and pedestrian traffic.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Street’ means a road that is situated in a city, town or small town.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A road may consist of different road types.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Public road’ means a national road, local road and a private road designated for public use. Public roads may be used by everybody while observing the restrictions established in legislation.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg8">
						<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Private road accessible to the public’ means a road that has a public function as determined by its owner and that is not a national or local road.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg9">
						<loigeNr>9</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(9)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Roads of the trans-European road network’ means roads identified by Regulation (EU) No 2024/1679 of the European Parliament and of the Council on Union guidelines for the development of the trans-European transport network, amending Regulations (EU) 2021/1153 and (EU) No 913/2010 and repealing Regulation (EU) No 1315/2013 (OJ L, 2024/1679, 28.06.2024).<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92lg10">
						<loigeNr>10</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(10)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, definitions of the terms related to the building and maintenance of roads and the location, in Estonian territory, of roads of the trans-European road network.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para92b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">92</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 92<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>National roads</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para92b1lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>’National road’ means a road owned by the state and designated as national road, or a private road designated as public road by the state. For national roads, the duties of the owner are performed by the Transport Administration.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92b1lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A road is designated as national road if it possesses the core characteristics of national roads – which first and foremost consist in the serving of international traffic and in ensuring a connection between the state’s various geographical areas as well as destinations of broad public interest or economic impact – and having regard to the road’s engineering solution, the nature of the traffic served and the general principle of ensuring unified traffic and road maintenance organisation on national roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92b1lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A road is designated as national road by an administrative decision of the Transport Administration.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para92b1lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The types of national roads are enacted by a regulation of the minister in charge of the policy sector.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para92b2">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="2">92</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 92<sup>2</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Allowing for construction of electronic communications infrastructure as part of national roads </paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para92b2lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The road management plan mentioned in subsection 1 of § 1<sup>1</sup>  of the Road Traffic Act makes provision for expenditure on construction of passive elements of the electronic communications network that are not required for the functioning of the road, except where this is not possible due to road safety requirements and on the condition that, for operating and managing such elements, a corresponding contract has been concluded with the foundation or electronic communications undertaking managing the network.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para92b3">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="3">92</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 92<sup>3</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Local roads</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para92b3lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>’Local road’ means a road that belongs to the municipality and is needed for the organisation of local road traffic or for the performance of other municipal tasks provided by subsections 1–2<sup>1</sup> of § 6 of the Local Government Organisation Act, or a private road that the municipality has dedicated to public use. A local road is designated by an administrative decision of the municipality. For local roads, the duties of the owner are performed by the municipality.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para93">
					<paragrahvNr>93</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 93.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Forest roads</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para93lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Forest road’ means a road that is situated on land retained in the ownership of the state and that is used predominantly for the management of public forests. A forest road may be used by anyone, unless the person or government agency who arranges the management of public forests has closed the forest road or a part of the road or restricted traffic on the road.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para93lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The person or government agency who arranges the management of public forests is authorised to enter into agreements concerning the use of forest roads and to arrange for the upkeep of such roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para93lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the requirements for the condition of forest roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para93lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A forest road must be marked by a name or indication.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para93lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The person or government agency who arranges the management of public forests arranges for the building and upkeep of forest roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para93lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The person or government agency who arranges the management of public forests may close a forest road or a part of the road or restrict traffic on the road:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para93lg6p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>if the load-bearing part of the road has deteriorated due to the thawing of the ground, or due to rain or other factors that significantly affect traffic - and traffic may damage the road, or traffic on the road is dangerous;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para93lg6p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for the purpose of fire safety;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para93lg6p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for the purpose of protecting the ecosystems of the forest;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para93lg6p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for the purpose of preventing the commission of an offence;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para93lg6p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>for the purpose of ensuring safety during forestry work or</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para93lg6p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>if the road is not needed for the management of public forests or for local traffic.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para93lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In order to close the forest road or restrict traffic, the person or government agency who arranges the management of public forests must install the required traffic control devices.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para93lg8">
						<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may enact, by means of a regulation, the requirements for the marking of forest roads and the rules for the road marking system.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para94">
					<paragrahvNr>94</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 94.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Acquisition of private roads in the public interest or appropriation of private roads for public use</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<muutmismarge>
						<avaldamismarge>
							<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
							<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-06-29</avaldamineKuupaev>
							<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
							<aktViide>129062018001</aktViide>
						</avaldamismarge>
						<joustumine>2018-07-01</joustumine>
					</muutmismarge>
					<loige id="para94lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A private road is designated for public use by the state or by the municipality in whose administrative territory the private road is situated.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para94lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Acquisition of a private road in the public interest or subjection of a private road to compulsory possession is decided, in accordance with the rules provided by the Acquisition of Immovables in Public Interest Act, by the state or by the municipality in whose administrative territory the private road is situated.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-06-29</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>129062018001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2018-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para94lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When a private road is designated for public use, the state or municipality assumes all obligations, rights and liability of the owner of the road. It is possible to stipulate, by a regulatory contract, that the obligations, rights and liability of the owner of the road remain vested in the owner of the private road. </tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-06-29</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>129062018001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2018-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para94lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Within 7 days from the entry into effect of the decision on designating a private road for public use, the state or municipality presents that decision and, in machine-readable form, the data concerning the road’s spatial dimensions, to the keeper of the Land Cadastre. </tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-06-29</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>129062018001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2018-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para95">
					<paragrahvNr>95</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 95.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Right of pre-emption</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para95lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where an item of immovable property is sold that is traversed by an existing or envisaged road that, according to the detailed spatial plan, is to be designated for public use, the municipality in whose administrative territory the item is situated has a right of pre-emption.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para95lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The municipality does not have a right of pre-emption where the item of property is sold to the owner's spouse, descendant, or parent, as well as to the owner's brother, sister, or any of their descendants or to the Republic of Estonia, as well as where the property that is sold constitutes apartment ownership rights, the right of superficies or the right of apartment superficies.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para95lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A note concerning the fact that the item of immovable property has been encumbered with the right of pre-emption mentioned in subsection 1 of this section is recorded in the third division of the Land Register entry for the item on an application by the municipality that brought into effect the detailed spatial plan that provides for designating the existing or envisaged road for public use. The recording of the note does not require the consent of the owner of the property. The application and the recorded note must cite this Code and this section and the detailed spatial plan that provides for designating the existing or envisaged road for public use.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para95lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the entry in the Land Register shows that the item of immovable property is encumbered with a right of pre-emption within the meaning of this section, the notary public, within five business days from authenticating the sales or other agreement that stipulates the obligation to acquire or transfer the item, transmits a notarially certified copy of the agreement by electronic means to the municipality in whose administrative territory the item or construction work that is being sold is situated, in order for the municipality to decide on the exercise of the right of pre-emption.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para95lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The right of pre-emption provided by this section may not be exercised in respect of an item of property that is sold by way of compulsory enforcement or as part of insolvency proceedings, as well as where the item of immovable property is subjected to acquisition in the public interest, including to compulsory acquisition. Where an auction is to be held in respect of an item of immovable property whose entry in the Land Register shows that it is encumbered with a right of pre-emption within the meaning of this section, the enforcement agent or trustee in bankruptcy transmits, at least ten days before the auction is held, the corresponding notice to the municipality in whose administrative territory the property is situated.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2018-06-29</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>129062018001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2018-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para96">
					<paragrahvNr>96</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 96.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Requirements for the building of roads</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para96lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The building or designing of tunnels whose length exceeds 500 metres is based on the requirements provied by Directive 2004/54/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council on minimum safety requirements for tunnels in the trans-European road network (OJ L 167, 30.04.2004, pp. 39–91).<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para96lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector may, by means of a regulation, enact the requirements for the building and designing of tunnels whose length exceeds 500 metres and to designate the authority responsible for ensuring the safety of the tunnel.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para96lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by means of a regulation, the quality requirements for the building of roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para97">
					<paragrahvNr>97</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 97.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Road maintenance</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para97lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Roads and any civil engineering works required for the functioning of the road must be maintained such that they conform to the requirements and such that the conditions for safe traffic are ensured.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, the requirements for the condition of roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>At level crossings, building and maintenance work on the intersection is performed and conditions for safe traffic are ensured by the owner of the road, the railway infrastructure manager or the owner or possessor of the railway within the extent of the item of immovable property in their possession, except for winter maintenance work that the owner of the road is under a duty perform for the entire area of the level crossing. The owner of the road, the railway infrastructure manager or any other owner or possessor of the railway conclude an agreement that stipulates the details pertaining to winter maintenance work.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg3b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where a bridge or overpass that is part of a road that does not possess the core characteristics of national roads has been constructed for crossing a public railway whose track gauge is 1435 mm, the duties of the owner of the bridge or overpass are performed by the Transport Administration. Regarding the section of road mentioned in the first sentence of this subsection, compliance of the road with requirements for its condition is ensured by the municipality – if obligations with regard to ensuring compliance of the section with requirements for its condition have not been allocated between the parties on the basis of an agreement to be concluded between the Transport Administration and the municipality.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>At the crossing of roads belonging to different owners, each owner is responsible, within their item of immovable property, for the condition of the road that is necessary for ensuring safe traffic.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The upkeep of a non-road civil engineering work, including a soil amelioration or hydro-technical civil engineering work, that is situated within the road and that is owned by another person is ensured by the owner of the non-road civil engineering work, which does not preclude liability of the owner of the road to the person who sustained harm due to the non-conformity of the road to the requirements for road condition. The owner of the non-road civil engineering work is liable to compensate the owner of the road in accordance with the rules established in the Law of Obligations Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In a city, town and small town, the owner of the land adjacent to the road must arrange the clearing of the pavement that runs between their item of immovable property and the carriageway, including snow clearing and gritting to an extent that allows for safe pedestrian traffic on the pavement.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The undertaking that maintains a national road is deemed a provider of the vital service mentioned in clause 4 of subsection 1<sup>1</sup> of § 36 of the Emergency Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062023001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2023-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg8">
						<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The undertaking that maintains a local road is deemed a provider of the vital service mentioned in clause 2 of subsection 4 of § 36 of the Emergency Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-10-08</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>108102024001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2024-10-18</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para97lg9">
						<loigeNr>9</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(9)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The undertaking that maintains a local road is deemed a provider of services of general economic interest for the purposes of the General Part of the Economic Activities Code Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2017-03-03</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>103032017001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2017-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para98">
					<paragrahvNr>98</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 98.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Owner oversight</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para98lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When building a road subject to the building permit requirement, owner oversight must be performed.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para99">
					<paragrahvNr>99</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 99.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building design documentation and design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para99lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are required for the creation of building design documentation concerning the building or extension of any road that is subject to the building permit requirement and that is mentioned in Annex 1 to this Code, provided the location of the road has not been identified by a spatial plan at the level of items of immovable property.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para99lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The design specifications for the road - with the exception of national roads - are issued by the municipality together with the requirements for traffic arrangements. Design specifications for national roads are issued by the Transport Administration.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para99lg2b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where design specifications are to be issued regarding a construction work for which both the municipality and the Transport Administration are competent to issue such specifications, the specifications are issued by the authority whose competence extends to the construction work that represents the majority of the envisaged solution.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para99lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When connecting to an existing road or constructing utility network lines within the road area, the building design documentation must be approved by the owner of the road. The owner of the road may stipulate requirements, above all, in respect of:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para99lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>materials;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para99lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>measurements;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para99lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>structural parameters;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para99lg3p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>technology;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para99lg3p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the location – where not identified by the spatial plan or design specifications.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para99lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation, standards for the design of roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para100">
					<paragrahvNr>100</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 100.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Documentation of the building work performed on roads</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para100lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The documents concerning building work performed on a national road must be handed over to the Transport Administration and the documents concerning building work performed on a local road must be handed over to the municipality.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para101">
					<paragrahvNr>101</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 101.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building notice and building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para101lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In order to perform building work on a road, a building notice is filed with the municipality, or the municipality issues a building permit.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para101lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In order to build a national road or a national road envisaged by spatial plans, the building notice is filed with the Transport Administration, or the Transport Administration issues the building permit.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para101lg2b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where a national designated spatial plan has been created for construction of a national road, the building permit to construct the road or any construction works connected to it is issued by the Transport Administration, or the building notice must be filed with the Transport Administration.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para101lg2b2">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="2">2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>2</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the building design documentation filed with the application for building permit concerning a road includes construction works for which both the municipality and the Transport Administration are competent to issue the permit, the permit is issued by the authority whose competence extends to the construction work that represents the majority of the envisaged solution.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para101lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the road is to be built together with other construction works with which it forms a functional whole, the authority to issue the building permit may consolidate the proceedings concerning the issuing of the relevant building permits.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para101b1">
					<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">101</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 101<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy notice, use and occupancy permit </paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para101b1lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where a national designated spatial plan has been created mainly for construction of a national road, the use and occupancy permit for any construction works connected to construction of the road is issued by the Transport Administration, or the use and occupancy notice must be filed with the Transport Administration.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para101b1lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the building design documentation filed with the application for use and occupancy permit includes construction works for which both the municipality and the Transport Administration are competent to issue the permit, the permit is issued by the authority whose competence extends to the construction work that represents the majority of the building design documentation.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para102">
					<paragrahvNr>102</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 102.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Audits</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para102lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The tasks of the competent entity provided for by Directive 2008/96/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council on road infrastructure safety management (OJ L 319, 29.11.2008, pp. 59–67) are performed with regard to national roads by the Transport Administration and with regard to local roads by the municipality. </tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2021-11-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>2</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130112021002</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2021-12-17</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para102lg1b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Within the framework of the tasks provided for by subsection 1 of this section, the competent entity also arranges the performance of road safety impact assessments, road safety audits, network-wide road safety assessments and periodic road safety inspections with regard to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg1b1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>roads that are part of the trans-European road network;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg1b1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>motorways and primary roads;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg1b1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>public-use roads built with funds from the European Union, except for roads providing access to a plot, pavements, foot paths, bicycle paths as well as foot and bicycle paths.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2021-11-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>2</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130112021002</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-12-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para102lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements for road safety impact assessments;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements for road safety audits;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements for network-wide road safety assessments;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements for periodic road safety inspections;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para102lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the curriculum for road safety auditor training courses.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2021-11-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>2</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130112021002</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-12-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para103">
					<paragrahvNr>103</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 103.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Register of Roads</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para103lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The purpose of the Register of Roads is ensure the presence of a complete and up-to-date dataset on public roads for the organisation of road maintenance and for the exercise of regulatory enforcement.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The constitutive regulations of the Register of Roads are enacted, by regulation, by the minister in charge of the policy sector; the regulations make provision for the rules for keeping the database, including, among other things:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the structure of the database;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>the specific dataset;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>data providers and the data to be received from them;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>rules for the filing of data;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>rules for access to and release of data;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>specific time limits for data retention;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>tasks of the controller;</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg2p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst><tavatekst>other organisational matters related to the keeping of the database.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst></sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The controller of the data in the Register of Roads is the Transport Administration.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The information in the Register includes:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg4p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>technical specifications of the road;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg4p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>specifications concerning the civil engineering works required for the functioning of the road;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg4p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>spatial data of the road;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg4p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>particulars of the undertaking performing road maintenance – where requested by the road owner.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Register of Roads consists of:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg5p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the data of national roads;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg5p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the data of local roads;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para103lg5p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the data of other roads – where requested by the road owner.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner of a road is obligated to file the particulars of the road within 30 days following acceptance of the road or following the issue of a use permit in respect of the road.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg8">
						<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Constitutive Regulations may also provide for the possibility of other roads, which are not regulated in this part of the Code or in this Code, being registered in the Register of Roads.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg9">
						<loigeNr>9</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(9)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The information in the Register of Roads is disseminated through the Register's website.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para103lg10">
						<loigeNr>10</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(10)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Data of the Register of Roads are retained for an unspecified period. The constitutive regulations of the register may provide shorter retention time limits.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk13">
				<peatykkNr>12</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 12]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Construction Works in Public Water Bodies</peatykkPealkiri>
				<jagu id="jg8">
					<jaguNr>1</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 1]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Scope of Application</jaguPealkiri>
					<muutmismarge>
						<avaldamismarge>
							<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
							<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
							<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
							<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
						</avaldamismarge>
						<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
					</muutmismarge>
					<paragrahv id="para104">
						<paragrahvNr>104</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 104.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para104lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The provisions of this Chapter apply to the building of construction works in a public water body, and to encumbering such a water body with a construction work that does not have a permanent connection to the shore.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para104lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Submerged cable lines, pipelines and other utility network lines and utility works that are connected to the shore, as well as construction works that are connected to the shore by means of submerged cable lines, pipelines and other utility network lines and utility works, are not deemed to constitute construction works that have a permanent connection to the shore.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para104lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The provisions of this Chapter do not apply to the deepening of water bodies, to navigation signs and to the building of bridges that form a part of the road.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para104lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Any monuments situated in public water bodies are subject to special rules provided by the Heritage Conservation Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para104lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where an offshore wind farm superficies licence provided for by subsection 1<sup>2</sup> of § 113<sup>1</sup> of this Code has been issued for the building of a construction work, building work does not require a building permit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para104lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A construction work built under an offshore wind farm superficies licence provided for by subsection 1<sup>2</sup> of § 113<sup>1</sup> of this Code is issued a use and occupancy permit if the construction work meets the requirements provided by legislation – first and foremost to those established for construction works – and to the offshore wind farm superficies licence provided for by the same subsection.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para104lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The offshore wind farm superficies licence provided for by this Chapter is subject to provisions governing proceedings on superficies licences without prejudice to special rules provided by this Chapter.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
				<jagu id="jg9">
					<jaguNr>2</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 2]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Building a Construction Work in a Public Water Body</jaguPealkiri>
					<muutmismarge>
						<avaldamismarge>
							<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
							<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
							<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
							<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
						</avaldamismarge>
						<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
					</muutmismarge>
					<paragrahv id="para105">
						<paragrahvNr>105</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 105.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para105lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Design specifications for construction works to be situated in a public water body and to have a permanent connection to the shore are issued by the municipality within whose administrative territory the shoreline item of immovable property that is to support the building of the construction work is situated.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para105lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Unless otherwise provided by law, design specifications are not required for creating building design documentation concerning construction works that do not have a permanent connection to the shore.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para105lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is needed, the municipality issues design specifications for the following construction works that do not have a permanent connection to the shore (hereinafter, <i>construction work functionally connected to the shore</i>):</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para105lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a harbour facility required to service water craft, including any quays, protection moles or breakwaters;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para105lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a water traffic facility that is functionally connected to the harbour;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para105lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a utility network line or utility work required to service the construction works mentioned in clauses 1 and 2 of this subsection;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para105lg3p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a civil engineering work that is to be situated in a public water body and that is required to service a construction work situated on the shore, except for any utility network lines or utility works that cross the national border or an administrative boundary between counties;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para105lg3p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a sport or recreation facility that is envisaged without a permanent connection to the shore and that is to service a bathing beach;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para105lg3p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>to a construction work such as a floating hotel, sauna, restaurant or any other such work that serves persons arriving from the shore.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para106">
						<paragrahvNr>106</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 106.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Building notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para106lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In order to build, in a public water body, a construction work that has a permanent connection to the shore or that is functionally connected to the shore, a building notice is filed with the municipality.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para106lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In order to build, in a public water body, a construction work that has no permanent connection to the shore, a building notice is filed with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para106lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In order to build, in a public water body, a construction work that has no permanent connection to the shore, a superficies licence is filed together with the building notice.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para107">
						<paragrahvNr>107</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 107.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Authority competent to issue building permits</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para107lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority to issue the building permit for building, in a public water body, a construction work that has a permanent connection to the shore or that is functionally connected to the shore is the municipality.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para107lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority to issue the building permit for building, in a public water body, a construction work that has no permanent connection to the shore is the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para108">
						<paragrahvNr>108</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 108.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Application for a building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para108lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Applications for a building permit concerning construction works that have a permanent connection to the shore or that have no such connection state, in addition to the particulars required under the General Part of this Code, the coordinates and surface area to be occupied by the construction work, or the coordinates and the surface area on which building work is to be performed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para108lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>For a construction work that will not have a permanent connection to the shore and that is mentioned in clauses 1–4 of subsection 3 of § 105 of this Code, a superficies licence must be applied for in accordance with § 113<sup>3</sup> of this Code before filing the application for a building permit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para108lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When filing an application for a building permit concerning a construction work that will not have a permanent connection to the shore, the requirements for applications for a superficies licence applicable by virtue of the General Part of this Code and by virtue of subsection 2 of § 113<sup>3</sup> are followed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para108lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where, in respect of the area identified in the application, other proceedings for the issue of a building permit or superficies licence have been opened, and the nature of the construction work to be built based on those proceedings is such as to rule out the issue, in respect of the area, of a second superficies licence, the competent authority may return the application for a building permit without considering it.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para109">
						<paragrahvNr>109</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 109.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Procedure for issuing building permits</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para109lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may, by way of ancillary requirements to the building permit for a construction work that is to be situated in a public water body and that will not have a permanent connection to the shore, in addition to the requirements contained in the General Part of this Code, establish:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para109lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the time limit for demolishing the construction work and removing it from the public water body, and the related requirements, or</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para109lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements connected to the use and operation mode of the construction work.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para109lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority refuses to issue a building permit for a construction work that is to be situated in a public water body and that will, or will not, have a permanent connection to the shore, in addition to the requirements contained in the General Part of this Code, under the requirements provided by § 113<sup>3</sup>.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para109lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para110">
						<paragrahvNr>110</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 110.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy notice</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para110lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In order to use and occupy a construction work that is situated in a public water body and that has a permanent connection to the shore or that is functionally connected to the shore, the use and occupancy notice is filed with the municipality.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para110lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In order to use and occupy a construction work that is situated in a public water body and that does not have a permanent connection to the shore, a use and occupancy notice is filed with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para110lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the building, in a public water body, of a construction work that has a permanent connection to the shore, led to a shift in the shoreline of the water body and to an increase in the surface area of the item of immovable property situated on the shore, the use and occupancy notice may be filed only after the shift of the shoreline and the increase of the item situated on the shore have been recorded in the Land Cadastre and in the Land Register.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para111">
						<paragrahvNr>111</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 111.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Authority competent to issue use and occupancy permits</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para111lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority to issue the use and occupancy permit in respect of a construction work that is situated in a public water body and has a permanent connection to the shore or that is functionally connected to the shore is the municipality.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para111lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority to issue the use and occupancy permit in respect of a construction work that is situated in a public water body and has no permanent connection to the shore is the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para112">
						<paragrahvNr>112</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 112.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Applications for the use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para112lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Applications for the use and occupancy permit concerning construction works that have a permanent connection to the shore or that have no such connection state the coordinates and surface area of the area occupied by the construction work or of the area on which building work was performed.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113">
						<paragrahvNr>113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Procedure for issuing the use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may, by way of ancillary requirements to the use and occupancy permit for a construction work that is situated in a public water body and that has or does not have a permanent connection to the shore, in addition to the requirements provided by the General Part of this Code, establish:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the time limit for demolishing the construction work and removing it from the public water body, and the related requirements, or</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>requirements related to the use and operation mode of the construction work.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority refuses to issue the use and occupancy permit for a construction work that is situated in a public water body and that has or does not have a permanent connection to the shore, in addition to the requirements contained in the General Part of this Code, if the construction work:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>contravenes the interests of national security;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>may disturb air traffic, vessel traffic on shipping lanes or in a harbour, or disturb the safe mooring of water craft;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>contravenes the conditions established in the superficies licence or</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>contravenes another public interest.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the building, in a public water body, of a construction work that has a permanent connection to the shore, led to a shift in the shoreline of the water body and to an increase in the surface area of the item of immovable property situated on the shore, the use and occupancy permit is issued only after the shift of the shoreline and the increase of the item situated on the shore have been recorded in the Land Cadastre and in the Land Register and when, in accordance with the Water Act, the fee for encumbering a public water body with a construction work has been paid.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may refuse to issue the use and occupancy permit for a construction work that is situated in a public water body and that does not have a permanent connection to the shore if the applicant is not a person of a member state of the European Union or the European Economic Area.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The use and occupancy permit for using and occupying a construction work that is situated in a public water body and that does not have a permanent connection to the shore is valid until expiry of the superficies licence on the basis of which the construction work was built, unless otherwise provided by the permit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
				<jagu id="jg10">
					<jaguNr>3</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 3]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Encumbering a Public Water Body with a Construction Work that Does Not Have a Permanent Connection to the Shore</jaguPealkiri>
					<muutmismarge>
						<avaldamismarge>
							<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
							<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
							<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
							<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
						</avaldamismarge>
						<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
					</muutmismarge>
					<paragrahv id="para113b1">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="1">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>1</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b1lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>‘Superficies licence’ means a right to encumber, for a specified period of time, a delimited part of a public water body and of the exclusive economic zone with a construction work that is permanently connected to the bottom of the water body or to the seabed but does not have a permanent connection to the shore. The state is not required to apply for a superficies licence to encumber a public water body and the exclusive economic zone with a construction work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b1lg1b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>An application for a superficies licence to encumber a public water body with an offshore wind farm may be filed in respect of an area that constitutes at least 75 square kilometres.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b1lg1b2">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="2">1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>2</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>‘Offshore wind farm superficies licence’ means a right to encumber, for a specified period of time, a delimited area in an inland sea, the territorial waters or the exclusive economic zone with a construction work that is permanently connected to the bottom of the water body or to the seabed, and provides a right to build an offshore wind farm that complies with the building design documentation based on which the superficies licence was issued, as well as a right to special use of water when building the wind farm.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b1lg1b3">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="3">1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>3</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The issuing of an offshore wind farm superficies licence rules out issuing a building permit and an environmental permit for special use of water (hereinafter, <i>water permit</i>) in relation to building the wind farm.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b1lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A construction work that has been built under a superficies licence and that is covered by that licence constitutes an essential part of the licence and belongs to the holder of the licence as the holder's property. Any construction works that are permanently connected to the bottom of a public water body but do not have permanent connection to the shore and do not possess a superficies licence – or whose superficies licence has expired or has been revoked – constitute an essential part of the public water body and belong to the state as the state’s property.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b1lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Unless otherwise provided by law, the superficies licence does not replace other permits prescribed by law that are required for building and using a construction work that constitutes an essential part of the licence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b1lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The area to be encumbered in the public water body is made up of the surface projection area of the construction work and of any civil engineering works required to service the construction work. Where construction works are built under a single superficies licence, the area to be encumbered is also deemed to include any distances of up to 1000 metres between the construction works, which are calculated based on the width dimension of the construction works. In the case of a wind power plant, the surface projection area is also deemed to include distances of up to 1000 metres between wind turbines that are part of the plant – calculated based on the width dimension of the turbines – as well as the ground projection area of any civil engineering works required to service the plant.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b1lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>This Subchapter does not apply to the dredging of public water bodies or to any navigation aids that are to be installed in such bodies.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b2">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="2">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>2</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Superficies licence proceedings commenced by the state</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b2lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The state may apply for a superficies licence in order to encumber a public water body with:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b2lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>an offshore wind farm;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b2lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a construction work intended to serve the purposes of an aquaculture-related commercial venture.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b2lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Within 18 months following the issuing of the superficies licence, the state arranges a public auction or a selective tender to transfer the licence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b2lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When conducting the public auction or selective tender, the administrator of state assets or a person authorised by the administrator follows the State Assets Act without prejudice to special rules provided by this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b2lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the state files an application for a superficies licence, any other such applications that have been filed for the same water body area are returned by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority (hereinafter in this Subchapter, <i>the competent authority</i>) without further consideration.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b2lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Section 113<sup>6</sup> does not apply in proceedings on an application for a superficies licence filed by the state.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b2lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The rules for public auctions and selective tenders of superficies licences for public water bodies are enacted by a regulation of the Government of the Republic.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b3">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="3">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>3</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Applying for a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b3lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a superficies licence is filed with the competent authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b3lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a superficies licence must contain the following particulars:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the purpose of use of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the maximum height and depth of the construction work and other technical particulars that are material in the case;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the number of construction works on the encumbered area and the ground projection area of the construction works;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the coordinates of the area to be encumbered in the public water body and the area's size in square metres;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where a public water body is to be encumbered with a power plant, the potential capacity of the plant and the system operator's technical requirements for its connection to the transmission network, except where the applicant is the system operator;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a list of envisaged investigations that the applicant intends to undertake in order for a decision to be made concerning the application;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the applied-for duration of the licence;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for a company or a non-profit association, a declaration certifying that the information filed with the Commercial Register or the Register of Non-Profit Associations and Foundations concerning the company's shareholders or members of the non-profit association, and its beneficial owners, is complete and accurate;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>particulars concerning the sources of funding intended to finance the completion and subsequent use of the construction work that constitutes the subject matter of the licence;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p10">
								<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where this is required by the competent authority, any other relevant information or documents related to the application;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg2p11">
								<alampunktNr>11</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[11)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>information concerning the novelty of the technology envisaged to be employed in innovation areas.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b3lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A map of the layout of the envisaged construction work and of any civil engineering works required for servicing the construction work, including submerged cable lines, and any other documents material to deciding on encumbering the public water body with the construction work are annexed to the application. When the investigations and the environmental impact assessment – as determined by the competent authority - have been performed, the applicant files the investigation reports and the environmental impact assessment report with the authority. Where, on having conducted the investigations and environmental impact assessment, new specifics are included in the documents initially annexed to the application, the applicant files the documents anew.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b3lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Within 180 days following the decision by which the environmental impact assessment report is found to meet the requirements, the applicant for an offshore wind farm superficies licence files, with the competent authority:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg3b1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>building design documentation that meets the requirements and technical particulars of the construction work – with the degree of detail sufficient for the granting of the right to build – and, where an expert assessment has been conducted concerning the building design documentation, also the expert assessment report;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg3b1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>particulars provided for by clauses 5–8 and 10–12 of subsection 1 of § 42 of the Act on the General Part of Environmental Code – unless such particulars have been sufficiently considered in the environmental impact assessment report;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b3lg3b1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>particulars provided for by the regulation enacted under subsection 7 of § 42 of the Act on the General Part of Environmental Code concerning the dredging of a water body or deposition – including dumping – of solid substances in such a body.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b3lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector my, by regulation, enact a list of particulars to be stated in applications for a superficies licence as well as specific requirements for such applications and their annexes.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b4">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="4">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>4</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Initiating superficies licence proceedings</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b4lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Initiation of, or refusal to initiate, superficies licence proceedings is decided by the competent authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b4lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Within the time limit provided by subsection 3 of § 113<sup>7</sup>, subsection 3 of § 113<sup>9</sup> or subsection 4 of § 113<sup>11</sup> of this Code, the competent authority makes a decision to initiate – or refuse to initiate – superficies licence proceedings. Where this is justified, the authority has a right to extend the time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b4lg2b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Superficies licence proceedings are initiated in the Register of Construction Works. Particulars and documents of the application are recorded in the Register by the competent authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-08-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b4lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When initiating superficies licence proceedings, the competent authority determines:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b4lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the person on whose application the proceedings are to be conducted;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b4lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>whether or not to initiate environmental impact assessment;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b4lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where this is needed, any investigations that the applicant for the superficies licence must conduct for a decision to be made concerning the issuing of the licence, and the time limits for such investigations;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b4lg3p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where this is needed, the requirements that are to be observed if other superficies licence proceedings have been initiated regarding the area identified in the application, or if - for a delimited area in the public water body named in the application - another valid superficies licence is present;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b4lg3p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>any other requirements that are needed.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b4lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where a water investigation mentioned in subsection 2 of § 236 of the Water Act is undertaken, the investigation is conducted following requirements provided by §§ 236, 237 and 243 of that Act. Where existing monitoring or investigation data are used, these must meet the requirements enacted under subsection 5 of § 53 of that Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b4lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may, on a reasoned application of the applicant for a superficies licence, extend the time limit for conducting any investigations or for complying with any other requirements determined on initiation of superficies licence proceedings.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b4lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The statutory fee for the superficies licence is paid within 30 days following the decision to initiate superficies licence proceedings.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b5">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="5">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>5</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Opinion of the relevant authority</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b5lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority refers an application for a superficies licence to the relevant authorities for an opinion. The time limit for providing an opinion is 30 days. If, within the set time limit, the relevant authority has not provided and opinion or extended the time limit, the application may be disposed of without that authority's opinion.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b5lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The relevant authority provides an opinion – in relation to the applicant and to the envisaged construction work – concerning their potential to endanger humans, property, the environment, national security, continuity of provision of a vital service, operation of the state's communications, a national defence object or the economy.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b5lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The relevant authority may request - from any person and from the applicant - any documents or additional information that it needs in order to form its opinion.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b5lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The relevant authority may propose that initiation of superficies licence proceedings be refused, where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b5lg4p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>in the authority's assessment, a significant adverse impact to human life, health, the environment or property is present that it is not possible to sufficiently avoid or alleviate;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b5lg4p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>based on the authority's assessment of potential dangers involved, the applicant or the envisaged construction work poses a danger to national security, continuity of provision of a vital service, operation of the state's communications, a national defence object or the economy and it is not possible to avoid the danger;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b5lg4p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the applicant has not, within the time limit set, produced the documents or additional information mentioned in subsection 3 of this section or made an application for the time limit to be extended;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b5lg4p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the documents or additional information produced under subsection 3 of this section are inaccurate and the applicant has not cured their defects within 30 days following having been issued the corresponding requirement by the relevant authority.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b6">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="6">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>6</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Notice of application for a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b6lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the relevant authority does not, under subsection 4 of § 113<sup>5</sup> of this Code, make a proposal to refuse initiation of the superficies licence and where circumstances provided for by subsections 1 and 2 of § 113<sup>11</sup> do not apply, the competent authority – prior to initiating superficies licence proceedings – publishes a notice in the official publication Ametlikud Teadaanded, in at least one daily newspaper of national circulation and on its website.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b6lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The notice states the particulars of the applicant and of the application and – according to § 113<sup>7</sup> of this Code – the rules and time limit for filing any parallel applications for a superficies licence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b6lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for a superficies licence is not subject to the provisions of subsections 1 and 2 of this section where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b6lg3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the application has been filed by an applicant who has won the competition mentioned in § 28<sup>1</sup> of the Spatial Planning Act or has borne the costs of creating the national designated spatial plan for the same area;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b6lg3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the delimited area of the water body identified in the application is compatible with the location determined as the most suitable for constructing a wind farm in the national designated spatial plan that has been brought into effect and</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b6lg3p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>no more than five years' time has elapsed following the bringing into effect of the national designated spatial plan.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b6lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The application for superficies licence is not subject to the provisions of subsections 1 and 2 of this section if it seeks to encumber a public water body with a submerged cable line, pipeline or other equivalent utility network or utility civil engineering work that has a connection to the shore.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b7">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="7">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>7</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Parallel application for a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b7lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Within 60 days following publication of the notice provided for by subsection 1 of § 113<sup>6</sup> of this Code, an interested party has a right to file their own application for a superficies licence meeting the requirements provided for by § 113<sup>3</sup> for encumbering the same delimited area of the public water body part with a construction work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b7lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where consideration of the application suggests an absence of interest by any other parties in filing a parallel application for a superficies licence, the competent authority has a right to reduce – but not to less than 30 days – the time limit provided by subsection 1 of this section for the filing of such applications.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b7lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>If no parallel application for a superficies licence has been filed within the time limit stated in the notice provided for by subsection 1 of § 113<sup>6</sup> of this Code, within 90 days following expiry of the time limit the competent authority makes a decision on initiating superficies licence proceedings. Where this is justified, the authority has a right to extend the time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b7lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where a parallel application for a superficies licence is filed within the time limit stated in the notice published in accordance with subsection 2 of § 113<sup>6</sup> of this Code and the construction work that the application envisages to encumber the delimited area of the public water body is substantially different from the construction work described in the first application, the competent authority, following the rules provided by § 113<sup>5</sup> of this Code, refers the parallel application to the relevant authorities for an opinion.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b8">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="8">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>8</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Amending an application for a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b8lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the area to be encumbered in the public water body, as stated in the application for a superficies licence, is amended before a decision is made on initiating superficies licence proceedings. The competent authority requests an opinion from the relevant authorities following the rules provided by § 113<sup>5</sup> of this Code. Where the amendment reduces the area to be encumbered, the competent authority may decide not to request such an opinion.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b8lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where this is justified, the area to be encumbered in the public water body – as stated in the application for a superficies licence – can be amended after the notice provided for by § 113<sup>6</sup> of this Code has been published and the procedure provided for by § 113<sup>9</sup> has taken place. Where, after publication of the notice, the location of the area is changed or the area is increased by more than 33 per cent, the competent authority publishes a new notice according to § 113<sup>6</sup> of this Code and, if any parallel applications are filed, deals with these according to subsection 4 of § 113<sup>7</sup> and § 113<sup>9</sup>.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b9">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="9">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>9</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Assessment of competing applications for a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b9lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where more than one application has been filed with the competent authority concerning a delimited area in a public water body (hereinafter, <i>competing application</i>), in relation to which under § 113<sup>11</sup> no grounds apply for refusing to initiate superficies licence proceedings, the proceedings are initiated on the application that meets the aspects provided by subsection 2 of this section. If these aspects are met by several competing applications, a competitive tender provided for by subsection 1 of § 113<sup>10</sup> of this Code is held. With respect to any other applications, the authority issues a refusal decision.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b9lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority assesses competing applications having regard to:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the opinion of the relevant authority;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the guidelines and requirements stated in the relevant spatial plans;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>environmental considerations;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>substance of the business activities of the applicant;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>economic strength of the applicant;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>economic profit that accrues to the state;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the period for erecting and using the construction work to be built on an area in a public water body;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the social usefulness of the project;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the purpose of use of the area in the public water body;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p10">
								<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>whether the project meets the aims provided for by the state's strategic documents;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p11">
								<alampunktNr>11</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[11)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the preferences of the state for use of the area in the public water body;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b9lg2p12">
								<alampunktNr>12</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[12)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the novelty of the technology envisaged to be employed in the innovation area defined in the spatial plan.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b9lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority makes the decision by which it initiates or refuses to initiate superficies licence proceedings within 90 days following approval of the results of assessment of applications for a superficies licence. Where this is justified, the authority has a right to extend the time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b9lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b10">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="10">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>10</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Initiating superficies licence proceedings by competitive tender</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b10lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where no refusal decision has been made under subsection 1 of § 113<sup>9</sup> of this Code, the competent authority – within 60 days following approval of the results of assessment of the applications – arranges an auction-based competitive tender (hereinafter, <i>competitive tender</i>) between the parties who filed the competing applications.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When it announces a competitive tender, the competent authority determines:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the starting price for the auction, set at 12,500 euros per square kilometre where the public water body is to be encumbered with a construction work that does not have a permanent connection to the shore but that is not an offshore wind farm, and at 15,000 euros per square kilometre where the public water body is to be encumbered with a wind power plant;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the amount of the deposit fee, which is two per cent of the starting price in the case of offshore wind farms and ten per cent in the case of other construction works;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>whether the competitive tender is held as an oral, written or electronic auction;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the requirements for bids.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The deposit fee is returned once the winner has emerged or the tender has been declared unsuccessful. The winner's deposit is deducted from the bid made in the auction.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The deposit fee is not returned to a person who caused the auction to be declared unsuccessful under clause 2 or 3 of subsection 7 of this section.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority does not admit to the competitive tender - as a participant in that tender - an applicant who filed a competing application if they have not paid the deposit fee within the time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority rejects a bid made by a participant if the bid does not comply with the requirements.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority declares a competitive tender unsuccessful where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg7p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the rules for conducting the tender have been violated;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg7p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>after the tender has taken place, it comes to light that the winner has filed false information;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg7p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>- when the winner does not, within the time limit, pay the amount they have bid or withdraws their application for a superficies licence - only one bid remains that complies with the requirements;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg7p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>no person has been registered as participant of the auction;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg7p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>no bids – or no bids that comply with requirements – have been filed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg7p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>at the auction, an arrangement between, or concerted activity of, participants came to light, which materially affected – or may have materially affected – the result of the auction;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b10lg7p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>other circumstances mentioned by the organiser in the terms or notice of the auction come to light.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg8">
							<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where a competitive tender is declared unsuccessful, the competent authority may arrange a new competitive tender within 30 days following the day on which the bids were opened. If the new tender is unsuccessful, the tender ends without a result.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg9">
							<loigeNr>9</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(9)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The person who filed a competing application and whose actions or omissions caused the competitive tender to be declared unsuccessful is not allowed to participate in a new competitive tender arranged under subsection 8 of this section and, with respect to their application, the competent authority makes a decision by which it refuses to initiate superficies licence proceedings.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg10">
							<loigeNr>10</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(10)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Superficies licence proceedings are initiated for the participant of the competitive tender who has bid the highest price in that tender and who, within the time limit determined in the notice of the tender, pays the amount they have bid.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg11">
							<loigeNr>11</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(11)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg12">
							<loigeNr>12</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(12)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Based on subsection 10 of this section, the competent authority ascertains the applicant for whom superficies licence proceedings are to be initiated, and – within 90 days following the applicant’s having been ascertained – makes a decision by which it initiates such proceedings. With respect to any other competing applications, the authority – within the same time limit – enters a decision by which it refuses to initiate the proceedings. Where this is justified, the authority may extend the time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg13">
							<loigeNr>13</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(13)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where circumstances provided for by § 113<sup>11</sup> of this Code come to light, superficies licence proceedings that were initiated by competitive tender may end with a refusal to issue the licence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b10lg14">
							<loigeNr>14</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(14)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The rules for initiating superficies licence proceedings by competitive tender are enacted by a regulation of the minister in charge of the policy sector.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2023-03-07</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>21</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>107032023021</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2023-03-17</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b11">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="11">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>11</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Refusing to initiate superficies licence proceedings</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b11lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where it is manifest that it is impossible to issue a superficies licence, the competent authority refuses to initiate superficies licence proceedings.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b11lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority also refuses to initiate superficies licence proceedings where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for the delimited area of the water body that is described in the application, proceedings have already been initiated for the issue of another superficies licence, and it is not possible to issue a second superficies licence for the area due to the nature of the construction work to be built under the superficies licence that may be issued as a result of such proceedings;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the application is contrary to a spatial plan that is in effect for the delimited area of the water body that is described in the application;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a spatial planning proceedings have been initiated in respect of the delimited area of the water body described in the application, and have not been completed;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a national designated spatial plan must be adopted in order to build the envisaged construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a significant adverse impact for human life, health, the environment or property is present that cannot be sufficiently avoided or alleviated;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the applicant or a person connected to the applicant or the envisaged construction work creates a danger to national security, to continuity of provision of a vital service, to operation of the state's communications, to a national defence object or the economy and the danger cannot be eliminated;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>regarding the applicant, circumstances are present that are provided for by clause 3 or 4 of subsection 4 of § 113<sup>5</sup> or by the third sentence of subsection 1 of § 113<sup>9</sup> or by subsection 9 or the second sentence of subsection 12 of § 113<sup>10</sup> or by clause 2, 4 or 6 of subsection 1 or by subsection 3 of § 113<sup>13</sup> of this Code;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b11lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the competitive tender arranged on the basis of § 113<sup>10</sup> of this Code has ended without a result.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b11lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The provision of clause 3 of subsection 2 of this section does not apply to a construction work provided for by subsection 2 of § 104 of this Code and to a temporary construction work if the applicant accepts that the superficies licence will be issued for the period of validity provided by subsection 4 of § 113<sup>14</sup>.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b11lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Unless otherwise provided for by this Code, within 90 days following emergence of a circumstance provided for by subsection 2 of this section the competent authority makes a decision by which it refuses to initiate superficies licence proceedings. Where this is justified, the authority has a right to extend that time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b12">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="12">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>12</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Issuing a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b12lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A superficies licence is issued by the competent authority electronically, in the Register of Construction Works.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-08-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When issuing a superficies licence, the following conditions of the licence are determined:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the licence holder;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the coordinates and size in square metres of the encumbered area in the public water body, including the area to be taken up by the envisaged construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the location of the construction work in the area encumbered;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the purpose of use of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the maximum authorised height and depth as well as any other important technical particulars of the construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the maximum authorised number of construction works and the maximum ground projection area that is authorised for a construction work;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the validity period of the licence;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p8">
								<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>restrictions on using the licence;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2p9">
								<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>any other necessary requirements.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg2b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In addition to conditions mentioned in subsection 2 of this section, conditions provided for by clauses 5 and 6 of subsection 3 of § 42 and of clause 2 of subsection 1 of § 109 of this Code, as well as by clauses 5–10, 12 and 15 of subsection 1 of § 193 of the Water Act may be set for the offshore wind farm superficies licence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg2b2">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="2">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>2</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority presents the particulars and documents provided for by subsection 3<sup>1</sup> of § 113<sup>3</sup> of this Code to the Environment Board for conditions to be set for the special use of water. The Board presents the conditions in writing within 30 days following reception of particulars and documents. </tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg2b3">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="3">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>3</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Having received the conditions provided for by subsection 2<sup>2</sup> of this section, the competent authority presents a proposal for the offshore wind farm superficies licence:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2b3p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for approval to the authority that, under legislation, holds competences relating to the subject matter of the building or water permit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b12lg2b3p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where this is needed, for an opinion to a person whose rights or interests may be affected by the construction work or its building.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg2b4">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="4">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>4</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where the authority or person has not, within 30 days of having received the proposal for the offshore wind farm superficies licence, refused to approve it or expressed an opinion, and has not requested an extension of the time limit, the authority is deemed to have tacitly approved the proposal or the person to have declined to express an opinion concerning it – unless otherwise provided for by law.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg2b5">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="5">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>5</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The offshore wind farm superficies licence is issued within 90 days following the filing of particulars and documents mentioned in subsection 3<sup>1</sup> of § 113<sup>3</sup> of this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In the course of superficies licence proceedings, based on the results of environmental impact assessment and of any investigations that have been conducted, the location of the area to be encumbered in a public water body may – by reference to the coordinates stated and compared to the area determined in the decision by which the proceedings were initiated – be modified, or the area may be increased, by up to 33 per cent, or reduced to a greater extent. The location of the area must not be modified or increased such that it comes to encompass a location for which a superficies licence has been issued or regarding which proceedings for issuing another superficies licence have been initiated, and it is not possible to realise both licences concurrently.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In superficies licence proceedings that do not include an assessment of environmental impact or the conduct of investigations, the making of changes provided for by subsection 3 of this section is permitted in other situations where this is justified.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b12lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority requests the opinion of the relevant authority under the rules provided by § 113<sup>5</sup> of this Code concerning any increase of or modification of location to the area to be encumbered in a public water body where such increase or modification exceeds 33 per cent.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b13">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="13">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>13</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Refusing to issue a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b13lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority refuses to issue a superficies licence where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b13lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the applicant has not fulfilled the requirements set in the decision to initiate superficies licence proceedings and has not applied for a new time limit for fulfilling these;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b13lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the conditions of the licence applied for are contrary to a superficies licence that is in effect;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b13lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the conditions of the licence applied for are contrary to a spatial plan that is in effect;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b13lg1p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the conditions of the licence applied for are contrary to the state's security interests;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b13lg1p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>there is a significant negative environmental impact that cannot be sufficiently avoided or alleviated;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b13lg1p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work that constitutes an essential part of the licence would interfere with air traffic, with vessel traffic in a fairway or port basin or with the safe berthing of water craft;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b13lg1p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>based on the results of superficies licence proceedings, the area to be encumbered in the public water body needs to be modified and the applicant does not accept the modifications.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b13lg1b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When issuing an offshore wind farm superficies licence, the grounds of refusal provided by clauses 1–3 of § 44 of this Code apply in addition to those stated in subsection 1 of this section.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b13lg1b2">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="2">1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>2</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When issuing an offshore wind farm superficies licence, the grounds of refusal to issue the permit provided by clauses 8–10 of subsection 3 of § 192 of the Water Act may be applied.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b13lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may also refuse to issue a superficies licence where reasonable doubts are present that the applicant, a person connected with the applicant or the envisaged construction work may endanger national security, continuity of provision of a vital service, operation of the state’s communications, a national defence object or the economy, or where the applicant for an offshore wind farm superficies licence has not complied with an obligation emanating from subsection 3<sup>1</sup> of § 113<sup>3</sup> of this Code and has not offered a valid reason to extend the time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b13lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may refuse to issue a superficies licence to a person who is not a citizen or legal person of Estonia or of a state party to the European Economic Area and whose superficies licence application is not aligned with material interests of the state.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b14">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="14">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>14</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Period of validity of a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b14lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A superficies licence is valid for up to 50 years. When determining the period of validity, the competent authority has regard to the type and purpose of use of the construction work.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b14lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may, on an application of the licence holder, extend a superficies licence by up to 50 years. An application for extending the licence is filed at least three months before expiry of the licence period.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b14lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Extending the period of validity of a superficies licence is subject to the provisions of § 113<sup>15</sup> of this Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b14lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where an application for a superficies licence is filed regarding an area in respect of which a spatial planning exercise has been initiated and the proceedings have not been concluded, the competent authority may issue a provisional superficies licence. The provisional licence is reviewed within one year following the bringing of the spatial plan into effect. If there are no incompatibilities between the provisional licence and the plan, the authority issues a superficies licence for a period of validity determined in accordance with subsection 1 of this section - on the same terms as those of the provisional licence. In the case of incompatibility with the plan, the superficies licence is not issued and the provisional licence lapses.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b15">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="15">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>15</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Varying the conditions of a superficies licence and suspending operations related to special use of water</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
						<loige id="para113b15lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may, on an application of the holder of the superficies licence or of its own motion, vary the conditions of the licence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b15lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may, on an application of the holder of the superficies licence, transfer the licence to another person.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b15lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority refuses to vary the conditions or particulars of a superficies licence where grounds for refusing to issue the licence apply.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b15lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In addition to provisions of subsections 1–3 of this section, the competent authority may vary the conditions of an offshore wind farm superficies licence that relate to the special use of water also on the basis of clause 2 of subsection 1 of § 59 of the Act on the General Part of Environmental Code.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b15lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The Environment Board may suspend – in their entirety or in part, and for up to three months – any operations related to the special use of water provided the following circumstances are present:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b15lg5p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>when erecting the offshore wind farm, the exercise of the right to special use of water entails a material disturbance to the environment, which could not have been foreseen when the licence was issued, or where the alleviation measures prescribed by the licence have not been sufficient;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b15lg5p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a causal link between he special use of water and the material disturbance has been proved and</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b15lg5p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the interest to refrain from suspending operations related to the special use of water is not an overriding one.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b16">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="16">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>16</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Passing of a superficies licence to the universal successor</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b16lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where a superficies licence has passed to another person under the rules of universal succession, the competent authority amends the licence holder particulars on an application of the universal successor or of its own motion.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b16lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>When a superficies licence passes to a universal successor, the other conditions of the licence remain unchanged.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b17">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="17">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>17</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Preliminary verification on transfer of a superficies licence or on transfer of a significant holding in a company that holds a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b17lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Before acquiring a superficies licence or a significant shareholding – within the meaning of § 9 of the Securities Market Act – in a company that holds a superficies licence, the person who wishes to acquire (below in this section, <i>the acquiring party</i>) such a licence or shareholding files an application with the competent authority that contains at least the following particulars:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b17lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the name, seat, registration number or personal identification number (or, where the person does not possess such a number, their date of birth), information concerning participation in another legal person or in a pool of assets and particulars concerning the person who is under the control of the acquiring party;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b17lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>a list of the shareholders of the legal person who is the acquiring party, information concerning the number of shares and of votes that belongs to each shareholder in the legal person or pool of assets, and particulars concerning persons who have control over shareholders of the acquiring party;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b17lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>for each member of the management board and of the supervisory board of the legal person who is the acquiring party, their given name and surname, personal identification number or, where the person does not possess such a number, their date of birth;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b17lg1p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>where the legal person who is the acquiring party is part of a consolidation group, a description of the structure of the group together with particulars concerning the size of the shareholdings of the undertakings that belong to the group.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b17lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>A legal person who is the acquiring party and who has been established and whose activities are mainly conducted outside Estonia files the particulars mentioned in subsection 1 of this section together with the annual report of its last financial year that has been translated into the Estonian or the English language and certified by a public document certificate (apostille).</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b17lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may require additional information in order to obtain more specific information in respect of or verify the particulars mentioned in subsections 1 and 2 of this section.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b17lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority requests the opinion of the relevant authorities concerning transfer, to another person, of a superficies licence or of a significant shareholding in a company that holds such a licence.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b17lg5">
							<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Having regard – in respect of the acquiring party – to the provisions of § 113<sup>13</sup> of this Code, the competent authority makes a decision by which it authorises the transfer of the superficies licence or the acquisition of a significant shareholding in a company that holds the licence, or refuses to authorise it. Where the authority has made a decision by which it refused to authorise the transfer or acquisition, the transfer or acquisition is prohibited and any transaction that violates the prohibition is void. </tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b17lg6">
							<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>On the transfer of a superficies licence to another person the competent authority amends the licence holder particulars on the licence. The other conditions of the licence remain unchanged on transfer.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b17lg7">
							<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The provisions of subsections 1–5 of this section also apply where a significant shareholding in a company that participates in superficies licence proceedings as a party to proceedings is transferred, or where a significant part of the enterprise belonging to the company passes to another person.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b18">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="18">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>18</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Revoking a superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b18lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may revoke a superficies licence of its own motion or on an application of the licence holder.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b18lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority revokes a superficies licence where:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b18lg2p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the licence holder has applied for this;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b18lg2p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the licence holder has materially violated the conditions of the licence;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b18lg2p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>within five years following the issue of the licence, no building permit has been issued to the licence holder – with the exception of the holder of an offshore wind farm superficies licence – in respect of the area covered by the licence, and the holder has not applied for an extension of that time limit;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b18lg2p4">
								<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>within two years following the destruction or becoming unfit for use of the construction work that constitutes an essential part of the licence, the licence holder has not filed an application for a building permit or applied for a new time limit to make such an application;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b18lg2p5">
								<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the construction work that constitutes an essential part of the licence poses a danger to human life, health, property, the environment, national security, continuity of provision of a vital service, operation of the state's communications, a national defence object or the economy;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b18lg2p6">
								<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the licence holder has been late paying the superficies fee on three consecutive due dates;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b18lg2p7">
								<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the licence holder has knowingly filed false particulars that had an impact on the decision to issue the licence.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b18lg2b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In addition to provisions of subsections 1 and 2 of this section, the competent authority may revoke an offshore wind farm superficies licence on the basis of clause 1 of subsection 2 of § 62 of the Act on the General Part of Environmental Code or of clause 4 of subsection 2 of § 194 of the Water Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b18lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may also revoke a superficies licence where a ground mentioned in subsection 2 of § 113<sup>13</sup> comes to light after the licence has been issued.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b18lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority may revoke the superficies licence in a situation where the holder of an offshore wind farm superficies licence has not, within seven years following the issuing of the licence, obtained a use and occupancy permit for the offshore wind farm for whose construction the superficies licence was applied for, and has not filed a reasoned application to extend the time limit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b18lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The competent authority decides on revoking the superficies licence after it has issued a compliance notice to the licence holder for the defects to be cured, and the holder has not complied with the notice.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b19">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="19">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>19</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Replacing a superficies licence with a right of superficies</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b19lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where, during the period of validity of a superficies licence, the part of the public water body encumbered with the licence permanently becomes land, the validity of the licence lapses as of the creation of the corresponding cadastral unit.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b19lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The holder of a superficies licence has a right to claim the creation - under the conditions of the superficies licence - of a right of superficies on the plot of land that has emerged. Proceedings on an application for creation of the right of superficies are conducted by the competent authority.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b20">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="20">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>20</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Removing a construction work from the water body on expiry of the superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b20lg1">
							<loigeNr/>
							<kuvatavNr/>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Unless the conditions of the superficies licence determine otherwise, the licence holder is obligated to remove a construction work that constitutes an essential part of the licence from the public water body when the period of validity of the licence expires.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
				<jagu id="jg11">
					<jaguNr>4</jaguNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Subchapter 4]]></kuvatavNr>
					<jaguPealkiri>Superficies Fee and Reporting</jaguPealkiri>
					<muutmismarge>
						<avaldamismarge>
							<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
							<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
							<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
							<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
						</avaldamismarge>
						<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
					</muutmismarge>
					<paragrahv id="para113b21">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="21">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>21</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Superficies fee</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b21lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where a public water body is encumbered with a construction work that does not have a permanent connection to the shore, the owner of the construction work must pay a yearly superficies fee.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b21lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The rate of the superficies fee is three per cent of the price calculated based on the Estonian average value of land whose zoned purpose corresponds to the purpose of use of the construction work and is calculated based on the encumbered area in the public water body.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b21lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b21lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Where a public water body is encumbered with a wind power plant, the rate of the superficies fee is 1.5 per cent of the product of the following two statistics:</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b21lg3b1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the quantity of electricity generated by the power plant, including both electricity supplied to the grid as well as electricity not connected to the grid, but not less than the rated capacity of the power plant multiplied by 4000;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b21lg3b1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the average day-ahead electricity price of the Estonian price region at the Nord Pool exchange for the relevant year.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2024-01-01</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b21lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>For the setting of superficies fees, the Land and Spatial Planning Board calculates the average value, by zoned purpose, of land in all of Estonia based on the results of a regular valuation of land conducted in accordance with the Land Valuation Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-12-04</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>104122024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2025-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b22">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="22">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>22</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Rules for paying the superficies fee</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b22lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The superficies fee starts to accrue from the day that follows the day on which the building permit was issued under the superficies licence or on which the offshore wind farm building permit was issued under subsection 1<sup>2</sup> of § 113<sup>1</sup> of this Code. The fee must be paid until the period of validity of the licence expires or the licence is revoked. Where the construction work is removed from the public water body after the licence period has expired or the licence has been revoked, the fee must be paid until the construction work has been removed from the water body.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b22lg1b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In a situation where, in addition to the superficies licence, the building of the construction wok does not require applying for the building permit, the superficies fee starts to accrue from the day that follows the day on which the building notice was filed, the environmental permit was issued or the activity that poses a risk to the aquatic environment was registered, depending on which of these occurred earlier, and the fee must be paid in accordance with subsection 2 of § 113<sup>21</sup> of this Code.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b22lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The holder of a superficies licence pays a superficies fee to the state once a year for the previous calendar year by the date provided by subsection 2 of § 216 of the Water Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b22lg2b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The holder of a superficies licence for an offshore wind farm provides to the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority (hereinafter, <i>the competent authority</i>), for the calendar year, the statistics mentioned in subsection 3<sup>1</sup> of § 113<sup>21</sup> of this Code by 31 January of the following year. The competent authority compares these to the statistics held by the transmission network operator.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b22lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>For the period following the issuing of the superficies licence until the beginning of intended use of the construction work, the superficies fee that must be paid is ten per cent of the rate provided by subsections 2 or 3 of § 113<sup>21</sup> of this Code. The fee must be paid at the full rate starting from the beginning of intended use of the construction work. </tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b22lg3b1">
							<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>In the case of an offshore wind farm, for the period from the issuing of the building permit or the superficies licence provided for by subsection 1<sup>2</sup> of § 113<sup>1</sup> of this Code until commencement of use, for intended purpose, of the construction work, the superficies fee must be paid at the rate of 0.15% of the minimum superficies fee provided by subsection 3<sup>1</sup> of § 113<sup>21</sup> of this Code. Superficies fee must be paid at the rate provided by subsection 3<sup>1</sup> of § 113<sup>21</sup> of this Code starting from commencement of use of the wind power plant for its intended purpose. For an offshore wind farm, commencement of use for intended purpose is deemed to take place at the time the farm commences generation of electricity.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b22lg4">
							<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The superficies fee is paid according to the rules provided by subsection 2 and subsections 4–6 of § 216 of the Water Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
					<paragrahv id="para113b23">
						<paragrahvNr ylaIndeks="23">113</paragrahvNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 113<sup>23</sup>.]]></kuvatavNr>
						<paragrahvPealkiri>Filing a report on the special use of water for an offshore wind farm superficies licence</paragrahvPealkiri>
						<loige id="para113b23lg1">
							<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The holder of an offshore wind farm superficies licence is obligated to file, once a year, with the authority provided by the regulation enacted under subsection 3 of § 195 of the Water Act and through the information system for environmental decisions, a water use report concerning the following operations: </tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para113b23lg1p1">
								<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the dredging of a water body, or the deposition, at the bottom of such a body, of dredging spoils in quantities starting from 100 m3;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b23lg1p2">
								<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>the deposition, in a water body, of solid substances in quantities starting from 100 m3;</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para113b23lg1p3">
								<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
								<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
								<sisuTekst>
									<tavatekst>dumping, in in quantities starting from 100 m3.</tavatekst>
								</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b23lg2">
							<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>Depending on authorised operation, the filing of the report filed under subsection 1 of this section is subject to requirements enacted under subsection 3 of § 194 of the Water Act.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</loige>
						<loige id="para113b23lg3">
							<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>The reporting obligation imposed on the basis of subsection 1 of this section ends when operations related to special use of water have been concluded and a report on the special use of water has been filed regarding these.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</loige>
					</paragrahv>
				</jagu>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk14">
				<peatykkNr>13</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 13]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Construction Works that Serve National Defence Purposes, Construction Works of Security Authorities and Infrastructure at the National Border</peatykkPealkiri>
				<muutmismarge>
					<avaldamismarge>
						<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
						<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
						<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
						<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
					</avaldamismarge>
					<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
				</muutmismarge>
				<paragrahv id="para114">
					<paragrahvNr>114</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 114.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para114lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The provisions of this Chapter apply to construction works that serve national defence purposes, to construction works of security authorities and to infrastructure at the national border. The provisions of this Chapter apply to roads serving national defence purposes.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para115">
					<paragrahvNr>115</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 115.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Definitions</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para115lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>For the purposes of this Code, ‘construction work that serves national defence purposes’ means any construction work belonging to the sphere of administration or in the possession of the sphere of administration of the Ministry of Defence, including any road that serves national defence purposes.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para115lg1b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In addition to what has been provided for by subsection 1 of this section, the Government of the Republic may, on a proposal of the minister in charge of the policy sector and based on the relevant threat assessment, designate as ‘construction work that serves national defence purposes’ a construction work that exists solely to ensure national security, including military defence of the state, or resolve an emergency situation.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 12.05.2026, 1 - entry into force 15.05.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para115lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>For the purposes of this Code, ‘construction work of a security authority’ means any construction work in the possession of a security authority.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para115lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>For the purposes of this Code, ‘infrastructure at the national border’ means construction works required for guarding the national border.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para116">
					<paragrahvNr>116</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 116.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Documentation of building work</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para116lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Government of the Republic enacts, by regulation, the requirements for the documenting of the construction works serving national defence purposes, of the construction works of security authorities and of infrastructure at the national border.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para117">
					<paragrahvNr>117</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 117.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Design specifications</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para117lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Design specifications are not required for the creation of building design documentation regarding construction works serving national defence purposes, construction works of security authorities and infrastructure at the national border, unless the construction works in question are envisaged to be erected in an area covered by a national designated spatial plan that has been brought into effect based on the pre-selection of the location.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2025-07-08</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>6</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>108072025006</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2025-07-18</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para118">
					<paragrahvNr>118</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 118.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Building notice and building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para118lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>To construct a construction work serving national defence purposes, a construction work of a security authority, or infrastructure at the national border, a building notice is filed with the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority. The building notice is not required for the building of a road that serves national defence purposes.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para118lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The building permit for a construction work serving national defence purposes, of a construction work of a security authority, or of infrastructure at the national border is issued by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority. The building permit is not required for the building of a road that serves national defence purposes.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para118lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In situations provided for by law, the building permit for a construction work serving national defence purposes and for a construction work of a security authority must respect the national designated spatial plan.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para118lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>No building permit must be applied for in order to demolish a temporary construction work serving national defence purposes.  A temporary construction work serving national defence purposes is demolished within one year after its use has ceased.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para119">
					<paragrahvNr>119</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 119.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy notice and use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para119lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The filing of a use and occupancy notice and the application for a use and occupancy permit is not required in order to use and occupy a construction work serving national defence purposes, a construction work of a security authority or infrastructure at the national border.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para119lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner notifies the commencement of the use and occupancy to the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority who enters the corresponding modification in the Register of Construction Works.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para120">
					<paragrahvNr>120</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 120.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Restrictions related to building work around a construction work serving national defence purposes and to the building of construction works that have a potential impact on the construction work serving national defence purposes</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para120lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In situations falling under this section, the erection, extension or remodelling of construction works is prohibited unless approved by the Ministry of Defence or by the central government authority designated by the minister in charge of the policy sector. The design specifications for erecting or extending a construction work or, in a situation provided for by clause 1<sup>1</sup> of this subsection or by clause 1 of subsection 2 of this section, for remodelling the construction work – or, where there is no obligation to issue such specifications, a proposal for the superficies licence or the application for building permit or the building notice – is presented for approval to the Ministry of Defence or the central government authority designated by the minister in charge of the policy sector if:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para120lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a construction work whose height exceeds 28 metres is envisaged;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para120lg1p1b1">
							<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the envisaged construction work is a wind turbine or a wind farm;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para120lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the envisaged construction work is situated in the protection zone of a construction work that serves national defence purposes;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para120lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the envisaged construction work may result in a reduction of the functional capacity of a construction work that serves national defence purposes.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para120lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The protection zone of a construction work serving national defence purposes extends, from the exterior wall of the building that serves national defence purposes or from the exterior boundary of the civil engineering work that serves those purposes or from the exterior boundary of the item of immovable property, to:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para120lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>up to 25 metres with respect to any construction work whose purpose of use may endanger the construction work that serves national defence purposes, or fulfilment of the functions of that construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para120lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>up to 300 metres in cities, towns and small towns with respect to any construction work that may affect the functional capacity of the construction work that serves national defence purposes;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para120lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>up to 2000 metres in villages with respect to any construction work that may affect the functional capacity of the construction work that serves national defence purposes.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para120lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Ministry of Defence or the central government authority designated by the minister in charge of the policy sector may, in the process of approving design specifications, establish, by way of ancillary requirements, the requirement to obtain further approvals concerning the application for building permit, and for use and occupancy permit, to be issued on the basis of such specifications.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para120lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Government of the Republic or, where it has delegated the corresponding authority to the minister in charge of the policy sector, that minister, enacts, by regulation, the functional capacity criteria of construction works that serve national defence purposes, the spatial extent of the restrictions and the particulars concerning construction works that affect the functional capacity of construction works that serve national defence purposes.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para120lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The provisions of this section do not apply to infrastructure at the national border.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para121">
					<paragrahvNr>121</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 121.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Restrictions related to building work around construction works of security authorities</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para121lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Any building work within 50 metres from the boundary fence of the construction work of a security authority or, where there is no boundary fence, the exterior wall of the building or the exterior boundary of the civil engineering work must be approved by the security authority. The security authority may prohibit building work on a building or on a civil engineering work where such building work may obstruct performance of the functions of the security authority or affect the security environment of the security authority’s construction work.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk15">
				<peatykkNr>14</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 14]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Drilled Wells, Boreholes and Dug Wells</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para122">
					<paragrahvNr>122</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 122.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Scope of application</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para122lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The provision of this Chapter apply to the designing, construction, commissioning, conservation and demolition of drilled wells, boreholes and dug wells.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para122lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The remodelling of drilled wells and boreholes is subject to §§ 123, 125 and 126 of this Code.</tavatekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2025-04-15</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>115042025001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2025-04-25</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para123">
					<paragrahvNr>123</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 123.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Definitions</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para123lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Drilled well’ means wells drilled for water extraction, for ground water monitoring and for thermal systems.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para123lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Borehole’ means a hole drilled for ground water monitoring and for thermal systems.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para123lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>‘Renovation of a drilled well or borehole’ means the addition of parts to the drilled well or borehole or the replacement of parts in order to improve the condition or repair a malfunction of the drilled well or borehole, or to extend its useful life.</tavatekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2025-04-15</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>115042025001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2025-04-25</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para124">
					<paragrahvNr>124</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 124.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Approval of the location of drilled wells and boreholes</paragrahvPealkiri><muutmismarge><tavatekst>Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026</tavatekst></muutmismarge>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para125">
					<paragrahvNr>125</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 125.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Documenting the building of drilled wells and boreholes</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para125lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A person who performs the work of drilling the well or borehole (hereinafter, <i>driller</i>) must during the drilling operations keep a drilling journal that records the following:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para125lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the location of the drilled well or borehole;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para125lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the time of performing the operation;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para125lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>a description of the work performed, including the method of drilling and of the performing of isolation;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para125lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the diameter of the drill and of the casing, and a description of the geological section in correspondence with the drilling depth;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para125lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the method used for sediment evacuation;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para125lg1p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the hydrogeological particulars of the drilled well or borehole.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para125lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When drilling operations are completed, the driller is required to file the particulars of the drilling journal with the Estonian Nature Information System in accordance with the rules made under subsection 6 of § 126 of this Code.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-05-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127052022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-06-06</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para126">
					<paragrahvNr>126</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 126.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Procedure for issuing building permits for drilled wells and boreholes</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para126lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority refers the application for building permit regarding a drilled well or borehole, or the building notice concerning the same, for approval to the Environment Board if:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the drilled well to be constructed or renovated is intended to be used to draw more than 10 cubic metres of groundwater in a 24-hour day or more than 150 cubic metres in a month or for more than 50 people;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the drilled well to be constructed or renovated is part of an open-loop geothermal system;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the drilled well or borehole to be constructed is part of a geothermal system and has a depth of more than 100 metres, or the geothermal system to be constructed has a designed capacity of 25 kilowatts or more;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the drilled well to be constructed extends into a Cambrian-Vendian or Ordovician-Cambrian aquifer complex or into an area of approved groundwater resources or into a groundwater reservoir, or where the drilled well to be renovated is situated in such an area;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the drilled well to be constructed is situated on a site of natural features that enjoys protected status under the Nature Conservation Act, or where the drilled well to be renovated is situated on such a site.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 15.04.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para126lg1b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Environment Board approves the application for building permit regarding a drilled well or borehole or the building notice concerning the same – or refuses to approve the application or notice – within ten days following reception of the application.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para126lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>When referring the application for approval, in addition to those required under the General Part of this Code, the following documents are annexed to the proposed building permit:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the design documentation of the sanitary protection zone of the water extraction point, where the creation of such documentation is required by legislation;</tavatekst>
								<muutmismarge>
									<avaldamismarge>
										<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
										<avaldamineKuupaev>2025-04-15</avaldamineKuupaev>
										<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
										<aktViide>115042025001</aktViide>
									</avaldamismarge>
									<joustumine>2025-04-25</joustumine>
								</muutmismarge>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the building design documentation of the drilled well or borehole.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para126lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Environment Board may refuse to grant approval – under subsection 1 of this section – to the application for a building permit for the drilled well or borehole, or to the building notice concerning the same, if:<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the building design documentation has been created by a person who has not been authorised to perform hydrogeological work for the creation of building design documentation for drilled wells or boreholes;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>in choosing the location of the drilled well or borehole, the geological or hydrogeological conditions of the area, the possibility of establishing a due sanitary protection zone, maintenance zone or supply zone or the impact radius of existing drilled wells or boreholes in the area have not been taken into account;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the depth of the drilled well as provided by its building design documentation does not allow for the water extraction rate or quality that is provided by the building design documentation;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the depth, structure or drilling method of the drilled well or borehole as provided by the building design documentation do not allow to observe the requirements of groundwater protection;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the choice of the aquifer to be opened by the drilled well or borehole as provided by the building design documentation is not justified given the purpose of using the water;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the extraction rate of the drilled well as provided by the building design documentation exceeds the approved unallocated reserve of groundwater in the area;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2025-04-15</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>115042025001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2025-04-25</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg3p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the applicant has not filed all required documents, or has knowingly filed false information.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para126lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In order to grant its approval to the application for building permit regarding a drilled well or borehole, or to the building notice concerning the same, the Environmental Board is authorised to require the applicant to conduct hydrological or hydrogeological investigations.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para126lg4b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In addition to the grounds provided by § 44 of this Code, the competent authority refuses to issue a building permit for a drilled well or borehole where: </tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg4b1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>under the solution envisaged for the drilled well by the building design documentation, the available quantity of groundwater in the area is exceeded;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg4b1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>under the solution envisaged for the drilled well by the building design documentation, the choice of aquifer is not justified based on the purpose for which the water is to be used;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
							<alampunkt id="para126lg4b1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the depth, design or drilling method of the drilled well or borehole as prescribed by the building design documentation do not guarantee compliance with groundwater protection requirements.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 15.04.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para126lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the total extraction rate provided for by the building design documentation of a drilled well or wells for public water supply exceeds 500 cubic metres per 24-hour day, the Environmental Board is authorised, when giving its approval to the application for the corresponding building permit, to require the applicant to create groundwater monitoring boreholes in order to monitor the status of water in the aquifer to be opened by the drilled well or wells for public water supply within the impact area of the groundwater extraction point or points.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para126lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The minister in charge of the policy sector enacts, by regulation:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg6p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the requirements concerning the design, construction, commissioning, renovation and demolition of dug wells;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-22</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>122022019001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2019-10-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg6p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>requirements for the construction, renovation and demolition of drilled wells and boreholes and requirements for the building design documentation, design and method of drilling;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 15.04.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg6p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the rules to govern the designing, constructing, commissioning, renovation, demolishing and conserving of drilled wells and boreholes;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg6p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the specific datasets of applications for building or use and occupancy permits as well as building and use and occupancy notices, and the form of the drilling journal location of drilled wells or boreholes, and the forms of notices, or the list of particulars to be filed by such notices, regarding demolition of drilled wells or boreholes;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para126lg6p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the rules for the filing, for entry in the Estonian Nature Information System, of the particulars of drilled wells or boreholes, and the datasets to be filed.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para127">
					<paragrahvNr>127</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 127.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Commissioning of drilled wells or boreholes</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para127lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the yield of the drilled well as provided by the building design documentation exceeds 10 cubic metres per 24-hour day or where the well is used by more than 50 people, the application for a use and occupancy permit concerning the well includes, in addition to what is required under the General Part of this Code, the following:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para127lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>an extract from the Estonian Nature Information System or a reference to the particulars recorded in that system regarding the drilled well in respect of which a use and occupancy permit is applied for;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-05-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127052022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-06-06</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para127lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the name, registration number or personal identification code and contact information of the person who performs owner oversight;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para127lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>maintenance instructions regarding the drilled well.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para127lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The application for a use and occupancy permit in respect of a drilled well for public water supply is referred for approval to the Health Board. The Board does not approve the application in respect of the drilled well or wells for public water supply if the water extracted from the well – after having been treated in accordance with the requirements – has a directly or indirectly negative effect on human health.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para127lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Where the yield of the drilled well as provided by the building design documentation is less than 10 cubic metres per 24-hour day or where the well is used by fewer than 50 people, the use and occupancy notice concerning the drilled well or borehole includes, in addition to what is required under the General Part of this Code, the following:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para127lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>an extract from the Estonian Nature Information System or a reference to the particulars recorded in that system regarding the drilled well;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-05-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127052022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-06-06</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para127lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the name, registration number or personal identification code and contact information of the person who performs owner oversight;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para127lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the maintenance instructions of the drilled well or borehole.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para128">
					<paragrahvNr>128</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 128.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Demolition of drilled wells or boreholes</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para128lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner of a drilled well or borehole or the owner of the land is required to demolish any drilled well or borehole that is unfit for use, poses a danger to the status of groundwater or no longer serves a useful purpose.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para128lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The competent authority refers the building design documentation concerning the demolition of a drilled well or borehole for approval to the Environmental Board.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para128lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Environmental Board is authorised to refuse to give approval to the building design documentation for demolishing a drilled well or borehole if:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para128lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the drilled well or borehole constitutes a national environment monitoring station;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para128lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the municipality has stated the reasons for the need for the drilled well as a reserve drinking-water well;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para128lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the building design documentation does not ensure compliance with the requirements of groundwater protection.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para128lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>[Repealed – RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para129">
					<paragrahvNr>129</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 129.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Conservation of drilled wells or boreholes</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para129lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The owner of the drilled well or borehole or the landowner is required to conserve any drilled well or borehole that has not been used for more than a year, and to notify this to the Environment Agency.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
		</osa>
		<osa id="o3">
			<osaNr>3</osaNr>
			<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Part 3]]></kuvatavNr>
			<osaPealkiri>REGULATORY ENFORCEMENT AND LIABILITY</osaPealkiri>
			<peatykk id="ptk16">
				<peatykkNr>15</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 15]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Regulatory Enforcement</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para130">
					<paragrahvNr>130</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 130.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Authority to perform regulatory enforcement</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para130lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Regulatory enforcement of compliance with the requirements provided by this Code and the legislation enacted under it is performed by the authorities mentioned in this section.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The municipality performs regulatory enforcement by carrying out the following functions:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg2p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verifying whether the building or the building design documentation of construction works, including any construction work that has a permanent connection or functional link to the shore, conforms to the detailed spatial plan, the relevant municipal designated spatial plan, the design specifications or other requirements applicable by reason of the location of the construction work;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg2p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verifying whether construction works or the building of construction works conforms to the requirements, including pre-use safety inspection of construction works;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg2p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verifying the existence of the building notice or building permit and the correspondence of the information stated in that notice or permit to actual facts;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg2p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verifying the existence of the use and occupancy notice or use and occupancy permit and the correspondence of the information stated in that notice or permit to actual facts;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg2p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verifying the correspondence of the upkeep and use and occupancy of construction works to the requirements applicable by reason of the purpose of their use;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg2p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verifying whether the requirements for the use and protection of local roads and for observance of protection zones of local roads are complied with.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority performs regulatory enforcement by carrying out the following functions:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the functions provided by clauses 2–5 of subsection 2 of this section in relation to verifying the conformity to the requirements of railway civil engineering works, of pressurised piping and pressurised containers, of electrical installations, of communication construction works, of lifts, cableways or other lifting equipment, of construction works that are situated in public water bodies and that do not have a permanent connection to the shore, of construction works that serve national defence purposes, of construction works of security authorities and of infrastructure at the national border;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2019-02-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>101022019003</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2019-02-11</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the functions provided by clauses 1–5 of subsection 2 of this section, above all in relation to verifying the safety of construction works after their use and occupancy has commenced;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of the conformity of construction works built on the basis of a national designated spatial plan to such a plan and to other requirements;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of compliance with the requirements for protection zones of construction works and for operations undertaken in such zones;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of compliance with the requirements established with respect to the energy performance of buildings, to energy performance certificates, to energy audits, to the recharging infrastructure of existing non-residential buildings and to the installation of automation systems for improving the energy performance of the heating or cooling systems of non-residential buildings as provided for by subsection 1 of § 69<sup>4</sup> of this Code;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p5b1">
							<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="1">5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of compliance with the requirements provided by Regulation (EU) 2024/1309 of the European Parliament and of the Council;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p5b2">
							<alampunktNr ylaIndeks="2">5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5<sup>2</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of the requirements for granting access to an active device of a mobile telephone network;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 21.11.2025, 1 - entry into force 01.01.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of compliance with the requirements applicable to undertakings and competent persons;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>in respect of buildings or parts of buildings which are in use and occupancy, verification of compliance with accessibility requirements;<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg3p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>checking the safety of wind turbines and wind farms.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Based on random sampling, the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority verifies whether the energy performance certificates issued during the year conform to the requirements. The number of energy performance certificates that are verified must be sufficiently high to constitute a representative sample on which to base the assessment of such certificates' conformity to the requirements.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg4b1">
						<loigeNr ylaIndeks="1">4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4<sup>1</sup>)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The verification conducted by the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority in respect of energy performance certificates includes:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg4b1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of input data that served as the basis for the issuing of the certificate and of the results shown on the certificate;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg4b1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>verification of the relevance of the input data and of the results and recommendations shown on the certificate;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg4b1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>comprehensive verification of input data that served as the basis for the issuing of the certificate and comprehensive verification of the relevance of the results and recommendations shown on the certificate, as well as, where possible, a visit to the building in order to verify whether the information shown on the certificate corresponds to the building in question.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-06-30</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>9</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>130062020009</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2020-07-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg5">
						<loigeNr>5</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(5)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Environment Board performs regulatory enforcement regarding the use of construction works in accordance with the requirements for environmental and nature protection, regarding radiation safety, regarding the sanitary protection zones and maintenance zones of drilled wells or boreholes and dug wells, regarding the requirements imposed on construction works in relation to the use of environmental protection resources and of natural resources in protected areas, in limited-conservation areas, in the conservation zones of individual protected natural features, in permanent habitats as well as regarding observance, in the shoreline or bankline building ban zones, of compliance with requirements concerning the special use of water in relation to an offshore wind farm that is built under an offshore wind farm superficies licence, and regarding observance, in a mineral deposit area, of the time limit for demolishing a renewable energy construction work according to the authorisation provided for by subsection 1 of § 15 or the approval provided for by subsection 7 of the same section of the Earth’s Crust Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2024-06-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>111062024001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2024-06-21</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg6">
						<loigeNr>6</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(6)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Transport Administration performs regulatory enforcement:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg6p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>in respect of the building of public roads, of the requirements concerning the condition of municipal roads, in respect of the protection zone and compliance with the requirements concerning the use and protection of national roads, and in respect of compliance with the requirements applicable in respect of undertakings connected to the building of roads and of competent persons;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg6p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>to the extent provided for by the Aviation Act, in respect of construction works situated in the immediate vicinity of aerodromes and heliports or in respect of construction works otherwise connected to the safety of aviation;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para130lg6p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3) ]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>in respect of compliance with the requirements related to the safety of maritime navigation and of navigation on inland waterways.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-12-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>110122020001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg7">
						<loigeNr>7</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(7)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<muutmismarge>
							<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-12-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>110122020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg8">
						<loigeNr>8</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(8)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Police officials perform regulatory enforcement of the requirements concerning the use and protection, and condition, of national roads and local roads where a violation of the requirements is identified in the course of police work.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg9">
						<loigeNr>9</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(9)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The National Heritage Board performs enforcement operations in accordance with the grounds and rules provided by the Heritage Conservation Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg10">
						<loigeNr>10</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(10)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Rescue Board performs regulatory enforcement in respect of compliance with fire safety requirements for construction works and with the requirements for shelters.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 02.10.2025, 2  ‒ entry into force 01.07.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg11">
						<loigeNr>11</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(11)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Health Board performs regulatory enforcement in respect of compliance with requirements concerning the safety of construction works for human health, provided the competence to perform enforcement regarding such requirements has been vested in the board by a law or by legislation enacted under a law.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 02.01.2025, 3 - entry into force 01.09.2025]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg12">
						<loigeNr>12</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(12)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<muutmismarge>
							<tavatekst>Repealed – </tavatekst>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-12-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>110122020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para130lg13">
						<loigeNr>13</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(13)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Agriculture and Food Board performs regulatory enforcement in respect of construction works used for the keeping of animals.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-07-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>101072020001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para131">
					<paragrahvNr>131</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 131.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Special measures authorised in relation to the exercise of regulatory enforcement</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para131lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A law enforcement agency may, when exercising regulatory enforcement as provided for by this Code, apply the special measures of regulatory enforcement provided by §§ 30, 31, 32, 49, 50, 51 and 52 of the Law Enforcement Act on the grounds and following the rules provided by that Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para132">
					<paragrahvNr>132</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 132.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Special rules concerning regulatory enforcement</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para132lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority may require the owner of the building to inform the public of the dangers connected with the building or, at the owner's expense, itself inform the public of those dangers.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para132lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The measure provided for by § 50 of the Law Enforcement Act may only be applied when entering a construction work or part of construction work or, after the placing on the market of a construction product, when entering the premises on which that product is stored, installed or sold, or on which the product is used.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para132lg3">
						<loigeNr>3</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(3)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A law enforcement agency takes the decision to demolish a construction work primarily when:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para132lg3p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the construction work does not conform to the requirements for construction works, and the non-conformity entails a significant or heightened danger;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para132lg3p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the unlawful building of the construction work has resulted in a permanent negative impact on the owner of the item of immovable property or the owners of the adjacent items, and that impact is excessively burdensome and it is not possible to sufficiently avoid or alleviate it;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para132lg3p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the time limit for demolishing the construction work has arrived and it is not possible to set a new time limit.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para132lg4">
						<loigeNr>4</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(4)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>A law enforcement body may, in order to ascertain whether a breach of public order has taken place, suspend the building, or use and occupancy, of the construction work also in situations where there is suspicion of a threat.<reavahetus/>[RT I, 11.07.2026, 3 – entry into force 01.08.2026]</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para133">
					<paragrahvNr>133</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 133.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Rate of non-compliance levy</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para133lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the event of non-compliance with a compliance notice, the law enforcement authority may impose a means of compelling compliance according to the rules provided by the Substitutional Performance and Non-Compliance Levies Act. The maximum rate of the non-compliance levy is 6400 euros for compelling a natural person and 450,000 euros for compelling a legal person to comply.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
			<peatykk id="ptk17">
				<peatykkNr>16</peatykkNr>
				<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[Chapter 16]]></kuvatavNr>
				<peatykkPealkiri>Liability</peatykkPealkiri>
				<paragrahv id="para134">
					<paragrahvNr>134</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 134.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Violation of requirements applicable to a construction work</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para134lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Violation of requirements applicable to a construction work, where the violation causes the construction work that has been built or is being built to become a danger to property, the environment, national security or a national defence object<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 300 fine units.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para134lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The same act, when committed by a legal person,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 100,000 euros.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para135">
					<paragrahvNr>135</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 135.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Violation of requirements applicable to building work</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para135lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Violation of the requirements applicable to building work, where the violation causes the construction work to become a danger to property, the environment, national security or a national defence object<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 300 fine units.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para135lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The same act, when committed by a legal person,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 100,000 euros.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para136">
					<paragrahvNr>136</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 136.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Designing a construction work that does not conform to requirements</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para136lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The issuing of building design documentation – where the construction work that has been built or is being built according to the the documentation – poses a danger to the life or health of humans, property, the environment, national security or a national defence object<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 300 fine units.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para136lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The same act, when committed by a legal person,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 100,000 euros.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para137">
					<paragrahvNr>137</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 137.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Violation of the obligation to retain data</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para137lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Failure to retain, in their full extent, for at least seven years, the building documentation or the particulars of the site investigations performed, the particulars concerning verification of the building design documentation, audit documentation, the particulars related to the issuing of energy performance certificates for buildings, or copies of these, where that failure significantly impedes assessment of the safety of a building,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 300 fine units.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para137lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The same act, when committed by a legal person,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 100,000 euros.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para138">
					<paragrahvNr>138</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 138.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Performance of building work without building permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para138lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The performance of building work without a building permit, where the building permit was required,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 300 fine units.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para138lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The same act, when committed by a legal person,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 100,000 euros.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para139">
					<paragrahvNr>139</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 139.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Use and occupancy without use and occupancy permit</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para139lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>Use and occupancy without a use and occupancy permit, where a building permit was required,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 300 fine units.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para139lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The same act, when committed by a legal person,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 100,000 euros.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para140">
					<paragrahvNr>140</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 140.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Illegal operations in the protection zone of the construction work</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para140lg1">
						<loigeNr>1</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(1)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>In the event of operations in the protection zone of the construction work that do not conform to the requirements, where this results in danger to the life or health of humans, to property or to the environment,<reavahetus/>such operations are punishable by a fine of up to 300 fine units.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
					<loige id="para140lg2">
						<loigeNr>2</loigeNr>
						<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[(2)]]></kuvatavNr>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The same act, when committed by a legal person,<reavahetus/>is punishable by a fine of up to 100,000 euros.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<muutmismarge>
							<avaldamismarge>
								<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
								<avaldamineKuupaev>2022-04-27</avaldamineKuupaev>
								<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
								<aktViide>127042022001</aktViide>
							</avaldamismarge>
							<joustumine>2022-05-07</joustumine>
						</muutmismarge>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para141">
					<paragrahvNr>141</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 141.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Proceedings</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para141lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>The out-of-court proceedings authority to deal with the misdemeanours provided by §§ 134–140 of this Code is – according to their sphere of competency –:</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p1">
							<alampunktNr>1</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[1)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the executive of the city or rural municipality;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p2">
							<alampunktNr>2</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[2)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the Consumer Protection and Technical Regulatory Authority;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p3">
							<alampunktNr>3</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[3)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the Environment Board;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-07-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>2</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>110072020002</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p4">
							<alampunktNr>4</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[4)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the Transport Administration;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-12-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>110122020001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p5">
							<alampunktNr>5</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[5)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the National Heritage Board;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p6">
							<alampunktNr>6</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[6)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the Rescue Board;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p7">
							<alampunktNr>7</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[7)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-12-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>110122020001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p8">
							<alampunktNr>8</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[8)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the Health Board;</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p9">
							<alampunktNr>9</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[9)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<sisuTekst>
								<tavatekst>the Agriculture and Food Board.</tavatekst>
							</sisuTekst>
							<muutmismarge>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-07-01</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>101072020001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
						<alampunkt id="para141lg1p10">
							<alampunktNr>10</alampunktNr>
							<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[10)]]></kuvatavNr>
							<muutmismarge>
								<tavatekst>repealed – </tavatekst>
								<avaldamismarge>
									<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
									<avaldamineKuupaev>2020-12-10</avaldamineKuupaev>
									<RTartikkel>1</RTartikkel>
									<aktViide>110122020001</aktViide>
								</avaldamismarge>
								<joustumine>2021-01-01</joustumine>
							</muutmismarge>
						</alampunkt>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
				<paragrahv id="para142">
					<paragrahvNr>142</paragrahvNr>
					<kuvatavNr><![CDATA[§ 142.]]></kuvatavNr>
					<paragrahvPealkiri>Entry into force of this Code</paragrahvPealkiri>
					<loige id="para142lg1">
						<loigeNr/>
						<kuvatavNr/>
						<sisuTekst>
							<tavatekst>This Code enters into force at the time specified in the Act to Implement the Building Code and the Spatial Planning Act.</tavatekst>
						</sisuTekst>
					</loige>
				</paragrahv>
			</peatykk>
		</osa>
	</sisu>
	<normtehnmarkus>
		<normtehnmarkusNr>1</normtehnmarkusNr>
		<normtehnmarkusTekst>Directive 2010/31/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council on the energy performance of buildings (OJ L 285, 31.10.2009, pp. 13–35), amended by Directive (EU) 2018/844 (OJ L 156, 19.06.2018, pp. 75–91) and by Regulation (EU) 2018/1999 (OJ L 328, 21.12.2018, pp. 1–77);<reavahetus/>Directive 2012/27/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council on energy efficiency amending Directives 2009/125/EC and 2010/30/EU and repealing Directives 2004/8/EC and 2006/32/EC (OJ L 315, 14.11.2012, pp. 1–56), amended by Directives 2013/12/EU (OJ L 141, 28.05.2013, pp. 28–29), (EU) 2018/844 (OJ L 156, 19.06.2018, pp. 75–91), (EU) 2018/2002 (OJ L 328, 21.12.2018, pp. 210–230) and (EU) 2019/944 (OJ L 158, 14.06.2018, pp. 125–199) and by Regulations (EU) 2018/1999 (OJ L 328, 21.12.2018, pp. 1–77) and (EU) 2019/826 (OJ L 137, 23.05.2019, pp. 3–9);<reavahetus/>Directive 2004/54/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council on minimum safety requirements for tunnels in the trans-European road network (OJ L 167, 30.04.2004, pp. 39–91), amended by Regulation (EU) 596/2009 (OJ L 188, 18.07.2009, pp. 14–92);<reavahetus/>Directive 2008/96/EU of the European Parliament and of the Council on road infrastructure safety management (OJ L 319, 29.11.2008, pp. 59–67), amended by Directive (EU) 2019/1936 (OJ L 305, 26.11.2019, pp. 1–16);<reavahetus/>Directive 2005/36/EC of the European Parliament and of the Council on the recognition of professional qualifications (OJ L 255, 30.09.2005, pp. 22–142), amended by Directives 2006/100/EC (OJ L 363, 20.12.2006, pp. 141–237), 2013/25/EU (OJ L 158, 10.06.2013, pp. 368–375) and 2013/55/EU (OJ L 354, 28.12.2013, pp. 132–170);<reavahetus/>Directive (EU) 2018/1972 of the European Parliament and of the Council establishing the European Electronic Communications Code (OJ L 321, 17.12.2018, pp. 36–214);<reavahetus/>Directive (EU) 2021/1187 of the European Parliament and of the Council on streamlining measures for advancing the realisation of the trans-European transport network (TEN-T) (OJ L 258, 20.07.2021, pp. 1–13);<reavahetus/>Directive (EU) 2022/2257 of the European Parliament and of the Council on the resilience of critical entities and repealing Directive 2008/114/EC (OJ L 333, 27.12.2022, pp. 164–198);<reavahetus/>Directive (EU) 2023/2413 of the European Parliament and of the Council amending Directive (EU) 2018/2001, Regulation (EU) 2018/1999 and Directive 98/70/EC as regards the promotion of energy from renewable sources, and repealing Council Directive (EU) 2015/652 (OJ L 2023/2413, 31.10.2023).
		</normtehnmarkusTekst>
		<muutmismarge>
			<avaldamismarge>
				<RTosa>RT I</RTosa>
				<avaldamineKuupaev>2026-07-11</avaldamineKuupaev>
				<RTartikkel>3</RTartikkel>
				<aktViide>111072026003</aktViide>
			</avaldamismarge>
			<joustumine>2026-08-01</joustumine>
		</muutmismarge>
	</normtehnmarkus>
